<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="MRK" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Mark</para>

<para style="toc1">Mark</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="MRK 1"/>

<para style="s">The Mission of John the Baptist</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 1:19–34</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 3:1–22</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 3:1–17</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Isaiah 40:1–5</char></note>The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ, Son of God.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, NE, MT, and TR; SBL and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The beginning of the gospel of Jesus Christ</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 1:2"/>Just as it has been written in Isaiah the prophet: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 1:2">“Behold, I send My messenger before Your face, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 1:2">who will prepare Your way.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">written in the prophets:</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Malachi 3:1; BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">before You</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 1:2"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 1:3"/>“A voice of one crying in the wilderness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 1:3">‘Prepare the way of the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 1:3">make straight His paths.’” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 40:3 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="MRK 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 1:4"/>John came baptizing in the wilderness<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">desert</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 12 and 13</char></note> and preaching a baptism of repentance unto forgiveness of sins. <verse eid="MRK 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 1:5"/>And all the region of Judea and all those of Jerusalem were going out to him, and they were being baptized<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they were all being baptized</char></note> by him in the Jordan River, confessing their sins. <verse eid="MRK 1:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 1:6"/>And John was clothed in camel’s hair, and a belt of leather <char style="add">was</char> around his waist, and he is eating locusts and wild honey. <verse eid="MRK 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 1:7"/>And he was proclaiming, saying, “The One mighter than I comes after me, of whom I am not sufficient, having stooped down, to loose the strap of His sandals. <verse eid="MRK 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 1:8"/>I baptized you⁺ in water,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">indeed</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> but He will baptize you⁺ in the Holy Spirit.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with water</char></note>” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with the Holy Spirit</char></note><verse eid="MRK 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 1:9"/>And it came to pass in those days <char style="add">that</char> Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee and was baptized in the Jordan by John. <verse eid="MRK 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 1:10"/>And immediately, going up out of the water, He saw the heavens being torn open and the Spirit descending like a dove to Him. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he saw</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see John 1:32–33</char></note><verse eid="MRK 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 1:11"/>And a voice came out of the heavens: “You are My Son, the Beloved; in You<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Beloved, in whom</char></note> I was well pleased.” <verse eid="MRK 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">The Temptation and Preaching of JesusMatthew 4:1–17</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 1:12"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 4:1–15</char></note>And immediately the Spirit drives Him out into the wilderness. <verse eid="MRK 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 1:13"/>And He was<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He was there</char></note> in the wilderness forty days being tempted by Satan, and He was with the wild animals, and the angels were ministering to Him. <verse eid="MRK 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 1:14"/>And after the delivering up of John, Jesus came into Galilee, proclaiming the gospel of God <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the gospel of the kingdom of God</char></note><verse eid="MRK 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 1:15"/>and saying, <char style="wj">“The time has been fulfilled, and the kingdom of God has drawn near. Repent and believe in the gospel!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 1:15"/></para>

<para style="s">The First DisciplesMatthew 4:18–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 1:16"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 1:35–42</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:1–11</char></note>And passing by the Sea of Galilee, He saw Simon and Andrew, the brother of Simon, casting a net into the sea; for they were fishermen. <verse eid="MRK 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 1:17"/>And Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“Come after Me, and I will make you⁺ to become fishers of men.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 1:18"/>And immediately, having left the nets, they followed Him. <verse eid="MRK 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 1:19"/>And having gone on a little,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from there</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> He saw James of Zebedee and his brother John. And they <char style="add">were</char> in the boat, mending the nets. <verse eid="MRK 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 1:20"/>And immediately He called them, and having left their father Zebedee in the boat with the hired men, they went away after Him. <verse eid="MRK 1:20"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Expels an Unclean SpiritLuke 4:31–37</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 1:21"/>And they go into Capernaum, and immediately on the Sabbaths, having entered into the synagogue, He was teaching. <verse eid="MRK 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 1:22"/>And they were astonished at His teaching, for He was teaching them as having authority, and not as the scribes. <verse eid="MRK 1:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 1:23"/>And immediately there was<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And there was</char></note> a man in their synagogue with an unclean spirit, and he cried out, <verse eid="MRK 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 1:24"/>saying,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Let us alone!</char></note> “What to us and to You, Jesus the Nazarene? Did You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!” <verse eid="MRK 1:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 1:25"/>And Jesus rebuked him, saying, <char style="wj">“Be silenced, and come out of him!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 1:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 1:26"/>And having thrown him into convulsions, and having cried in a loud voice, the unclean spirit came out of him. <verse eid="MRK 1:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 1:27"/>And all were amazed, so as to question among themselves, saying, “What is this? A new teaching with authority!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">What new teaching with authority that</char></note> He commands even the unclean spirits, and they obey Him!” <verse eid="MRK 1:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 1:28"/>And the news of Him immediately went out everywhere into all the surrounding region of Galilee. <verse eid="MRK 1:28"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals at Peter’s HouseMatthew 8:14–17</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 1:29"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 4:38–41</char></note>And immediately, having gone out of the synagogue, they went into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John. <verse eid="MRK 1:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 1:30"/>And the mother-in-law of Simon was lying sick, having a fever, and immediately they speak to Him about her. <verse eid="MRK 1:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 1:31"/>And having come near, He raised her up, having taken hold of the hand. And the fever<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Immediately</char></note> left her, and she was serving them. <verse eid="MRK 1:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 1:32"/>Now evening having come, when the sun set, they were bringing to Him all those being ill and those being demon-possessed. <verse eid="MRK 1:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 1:33"/>And all the city was gathered together at the door. <verse eid="MRK 1:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 1:34"/>And He healed many ill having various diseases, and He cast out many demons. And He was not allowing the demons to speak, because they knew Him.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, F35, WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they knew that He was the Christ</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 1:34"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Prays and PreachesLuke 4:42–44</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 1:35"/>And having risen up early, very much in the night, He went out and went away into a wilderness place, and there He was praying. <verse eid="MRK 1:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 1:36"/>And Simon and those with him went after Him. <verse eid="MRK 1:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 1:37"/>And having found Him, also they say to Him, “Everyone seeks You!” <verse eid="MRK 1:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 1:38"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Let us go another way into the neighboring towns, so that I might preach there also; for I came out for this.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 1:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 1:39"/>And He went preaching in their synagogues in all Galilee, and casting out demons. <verse eid="MRK 1:39"/></para>

<para style="s">The Leper’s PrayerLeviticus 14:1–32</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 1:40"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:12–16</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 8:1–4</char></note>And a leper<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A </char><char style="fq" closed="false">leper</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> was one afflicted with a skin disease. See Leviticus 13.</char></note> comes to Him, imploring Him and falling on his knees,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and kneeling before Him</char></note> and saying to Him, “If You are willing, You are able to cleanse me.” <verse eid="MRK 1:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 1:41"/>And having been moved with compassion,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Moved with indignation</char></note> having stretched out His hand, He touched him and, He says to him, <char style="wj">“I am willing; be cleansed!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 1:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 1:42"/>And<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">when He had said this</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> immediately the leprosy went away from him, and he was cleansed. <verse eid="MRK 1:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 1:43"/>And having sternly warned him, immediately He sent him out. <verse eid="MRK 1:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 1:44"/>And He says to him, <char style="wj">“See that you say nothing to anyone. But go, show yourself to the priest, and offer concerning your cleansing what Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Leviticus 14:1–32.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 1:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 1:45"/>But he, having gone out, began to proclaim much and to spread abroad the word, so that He was no longer able to enter openly into a city, but He was out in wilderness places. And they were coming to Him from everywhere. <verse eid="MRK 1:45"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="MRK 2"/>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals a Paralytic</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 2:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:17–26</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 9:1–8</char></note>And He having entered again into Capernaum after <char style="add">some</char> days, it was heard that He is in the house. <verse eid="MRK 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 2:2"/>And<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">immediately</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> many were gathered together, so as to have no more space, not even at the door. And He was speaking the word to them. <verse eid="MRK 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 2:3"/>And they come, bringing to Him a paralytic, being carried by four. <verse eid="MRK 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 2:4"/>And not being able to bring <char style="add">him</char> to Him through the crowd, they unroofed the roof where He was, and having dug <char style="add">it</char> out, they let down the mat on which the paralytic was lying. <verse eid="MRK 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 2:5"/>And Jesus, having seen their faith, says to the paralytic, <char style="wj">“Child, your sins are forgiven.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">forgiven you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 2:6"/>But there were some of the scribes sitting there and reasoning in their hearts, <verse eid="MRK 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 2:7"/>“Why does this <char style="add">man</char> speak thus? He blasphemes!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Why does this man speak blasphemies?</char></note> Who is able to forgive sins except One—God?” <verse eid="MRK 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 2:8"/>And immediately Jesus, having known in His spirit that they are reasoning thus in themselves, says to them, <char style="wj">“Why do you⁺ reason these things in your⁺ hearts? </char><verse eid="MRK 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 2:9"/><char style="wj">Which is easier: to say to the paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">forgiven you</char></note><char style="wj">’ or to say, ‘Arise, and take up your mat, and walk’? </char><verse eid="MRK 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 2:10"/><char style="wj">But so that you⁺ may know that the Son of Man has authority to forgive sins on the earth...”</char> He says to the paralytic, <verse eid="MRK 2:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 2:11"/><char style="wj">“I say to you, arise, take up your mat, and go to your house.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 2:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 2:12"/>And he arose, and immediately, having taken up the mat, he went out before all, so as for all to be amazed and to glorify God, saying, “Never thus did we see!” <verse eid="MRK 2:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Calls LeviMatthew 9:9–13</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 2:13"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:27–32</char></note>And He went out again beside the sea. And all the crowd was coming to Him, and He taught them. <verse eid="MRK 2:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 2:14"/>And passing by, He saw Levi the <char style="add">son</char> of Alphaeus sitting at the tax booth, and He says to him, <char style="wj">“Follow Me.”</char> And having risen up, he followed Him. <verse eid="MRK 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 2:15"/>And it came to pass, <char style="add">in</char> His reclining in his house, that many tax collectors and sinners were reclining with Jesus and His disciples; for there were many, and they were following Him. <verse eid="MRK 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 2:16"/>And the scribes of the Pharisees,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the scribes and Pharisees</char></note> having seen that He eats with the sinners and tax collectors,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with tax collectors and sinners</char></note> were saying to His disciples, “Why does He eat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and drink</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Luke 5:30.</char></note> with the tax collectors and sinners?” <verse eid="MRK 2:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 2:17"/>And Jesus, having heard, says to them, <char style="wj">“Those being strong have no need of a physician, rather those being ill. I did not come to call the righteous, but sinners.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to repentance</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 2:17"/></para>

<para style="s">Questions about FastingMatthew 9:14–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 2:18"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:33–35</char></note>And the disciples of John and the Pharisees<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the disciples of John and of the Pharisees</char></note> were fasting. And they come and say to Him, “Why do the disciples of John and the disciples of the Pharisees fast, but Your⁺ disciples do not fast?” <verse eid="MRK 2:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 2:19"/>And Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“Are the sons of the bridechamber able to fast while the bridegroom is with them? As long a time as they have the bridegroom with them, they are not able to fast. </char><verse eid="MRK 2:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 2:20"/><char style="wj">But days will come when the bridegroom shall have been taken away from them, and then they will fast in that day.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in those days</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 2:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Patches and the WineskinsMatthew 9:16–17</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 2:21"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 5:36–39</char></note>No one sews a patch of unshrunk cloth on an old garment. and if otherwise, the filling up pulls away from it, the new from the old, and a worse tear happens. <verse eid="MRK 2:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 2:22"/>And no one puts new wine into old wineskins. and if otherwise, the wine will burst the wineskins, and the wine is destroyed—and the wineskins.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the new wine will burst the skins, the wine will spill out, and the wineskins will be ruined</char></note> But new wine <char style="add">is put</char> into new wineskins.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Tischendorf does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">But new wine is put into new wineskins</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 2:22"/></para>

<para style="s">The Lord of the Sabbath1 Samuel 21:1–7</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 2:23"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 6:1–5</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 12:1–8</char></note>And it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> He is passing along through the grainfields on the Sabbaths, and His disciples began to make <char style="add">their</char> way, plucking the heads of grain. <verse eid="MRK 2:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 2:24"/>And the Pharisees were saying to Him, “Behold, why do they <char style="add">do</char> on the Sabbaths what is not lawful?” <verse eid="MRK 2:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 2:25"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Did you⁺ never read what David did when he had need and was hungry, he and those with him: </char><verse eid="MRK 2:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 2:26"/><char style="wj">how he entered into the house of God in the time of Abiathar the high priest, and he ate the loaves of the presentation,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Bread of the Presence</char></note><char style="wj"> which is not lawful to eat, except for the priests—and he gave also to those being with him?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 2:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 2:27"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“The Sabbath was made on account of the man, and not the man on account of the Sabbath. </char><verse eid="MRK 2:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 2:28"/><char style="wj">So then, the Son of Man is Lord even of the Sabbath.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 2:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="MRK 3"/>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals on the Sabbath</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 3:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 6:6–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 12:9–14</char></note>And He entered into the synagogue<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a synagogue</char></note> again, and a man having a withered hand was there. <verse eid="MRK 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 3:2"/>And they were watching Him, whether He will heal him on the Sabbaths, so that they might accuse Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 3:3"/>And He says to the man having the withered hand, <char style="wj">“Arise into the midst.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 3:4"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Is it lawful on the Sabbaths to do good or to do evil, to save life or to kill?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 3:4">But they were silent. <verse eid="MRK 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 3:5"/>And having looked around at them with anger, being grieved at the hardness of their heart, He says to the man, <char style="wj">“Stretch out your hand.”</char> And he stretched <char style="add">it</char> out, and his hand was restored.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as sound as the other</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 3:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 3:6"/>And the Pharisees, having gone out, immediately were taking counsel with the Herodians against Him, how they might destroy Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:6"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals the MultitudesMatthew 4:23–25</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 3:7"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 6:17–19</char></note>And Jesus withdrew with His disciples to the sea, and a great multitude from Galilee followed, and from Judea, <verse eid="MRK 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 3:8"/>and from Jerusalem, and from Idumea, and beyond the Jordan, and around Tyre and Sidon. A great multitude, having heard how much He was doing, came to Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 3:9"/>And He spoke to His disciples so that a boat may wait on Him because of the crowd, so that they might not press upon Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 3:10"/>For He healed many, so as for as many as had afflictions to fall upon Him so that they might touch Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 3:11"/>And the unclean spirits, when they were seeing Him, were falling down before Him and crying out, saying, “You are the Son of God!” <verse eid="MRK 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 3:12"/>And He was warning them much that they should not make Him known. <verse eid="MRK 3:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Twelve ApostlesMatthew 10:1–4</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 3:13"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 6:12–16</char></note>And He goes up onto the mountain, and He summons those whom He Himself was wanting, and they went away to Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 3:14"/>And He appointed twelve, whom also He named apostles,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, NE, BYZ, and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">whom also He named apostles</char></note> that they might be with Him and that He might send them to preach <verse eid="MRK 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 3:15"/>and to have authority<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to heal sicknesses and</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to cast out demons. <verse eid="MRK 3:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 3:16"/>And He appointed the Twelve:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And He appointed the Twelve</char></note> And to Simon He added the name Peter, <verse eid="MRK 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 3:17"/>and James the <char style="add">son</char> of Zebedee and John the brother of James, and He added to them the name Boanerges, which is Sons of Thunder, <verse eid="MRK 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 3:18"/>and Andrew, and Philip, and Bartholomew, and Matthew, and Thomas, and James the <char style="add">son</char> of Alphaeus, and Thaddaeus, and Simon the Cananean,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Simon the Zealot</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Simon the Cananite</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 3:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 3:19"/>and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:19"/></para>

<para style="s">A House DividedMatthew 12:22–30</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 3:20"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 11:14–23</char></note>And He comes to a house<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Then they went into a house</char></note> and a crowd comes together again, so that not even are they able to eat bread. <verse eid="MRK 3:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 3:21"/>And having heard, those belonging to Him went out to seize Him; for they were saying that He was out of His mind. <verse eid="MRK 3:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 3:22"/>And the scribes, those from Jerusalem, having come down, were saying, “He has Beelzebul,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Beezeboul</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Vulgate </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Beelzebub</char></note>” and, “By the ruler of the demons He casts out the demons.” <verse eid="MRK 3:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 3:23"/>And having summoned them, He was saying to them in parables, <char style="wj">“How is Satan able to cast out Satan? </char><verse eid="MRK 3:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 3:24"/><char style="wj">And if a kingdom may be divided against itself, that kingdom is not able to stand. </char><verse eid="MRK 3:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 3:25"/><char style="wj">And if a house may be divided against itself, that house will not be able to stand. </char><verse eid="MRK 3:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 3:26"/><char style="wj">And if Satan rose up against himself and was divided, he is not able to stand, but he has an end. </char><verse eid="MRK 3:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 3:27"/><char style="wj">But no one is able, having entered into the house of the strong man, to plunder his goods, unless first he should bind the strong man. And then he will plunder his house. </char><verse eid="MRK 3:27"/></para>

<para style="s">The Unpardonable SinMatthew 12:31–32</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 3:28"/>Truly I say to you⁺ that all sins and blasphemies will be forgiven the sons of men, as many as they may blaspheme. <verse eid="MRK 3:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 3:29"/>But whoever may blaspheme in regard to the Holy Spirit does not have forgiveness to the age, but is guilty <char style="add">of</char> eternal sin.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is in danger of eternal damnation</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">is subject to eternal judgment</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 3:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 3:30"/>For they were saying, “He has an unclean spirit.” <verse eid="MRK 3:30"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus’ Mother and BrothersMatthew 12:46–50</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 3:31"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:19–21</char></note>And His mother and His brothers<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His brothers and mother</char></note> come, and standing outside, they sent to Him, calling Him. <verse eid="MRK 3:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 3:32"/>And a crowd was sitting around Him, and they say to Him, “Behold, Your mother and Your brothers<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE, NA, and MT include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Your sisters</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> outside seek You.” <verse eid="MRK 3:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 3:33"/>And answering them, He says, <char style="wj">“Who are My mother and My brothers?</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Who is My mother, or who are My brothers?</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 3:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 3:34"/>And having looked around at those sitting around Him in a circle, He says, <char style="wj">“Behold, My mother and My brothers! </char><verse eid="MRK 3:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 3:35"/><char style="wj">For whoever shall do the will of God, this is My brother and sister</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and My sister</char></note><char style="wj"> and mother.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and My mother</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 3:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="MRK 4"/>

<para style="s">The Parable of the Sower</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 4:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:4–8</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 13:1–9</char></note>And again He began to teach beside the sea, and a very great crowd gathered together to Him, so that He, having entered into a boat,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the boat</char></note> sat down in the sea, and all the crowd was close to the sea, on the land. <verse eid="MRK 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 4:2"/>And He was teaching them many things in parables, and He was saying to them in His teaching, <verse eid="MRK 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 4:3"/><char style="wj">“Listen! Behold, the one sowing went out to sow. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 4:4"/><char style="wj">And it came to pass in the sowing that some indeed fell along the path, and the birds</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the birds of the air</char></note><char style="wj"> came and devoured it. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 4:5"/>And other fell upon the rocky <char style="add">place</char>, where it did not have much soil, and immediately it sprang up because of <char style="add">it</char> not having depth of soil. <verse eid="MRK 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 4:6"/>And when the sun rose, it was scorched, and because of having no root, it withered. <verse eid="MRK 4:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 4:7"/>And other fell among the thorns, and the thorns came up and choked it, and it gave no fruit. <verse eid="MRK 4:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 4:8"/>And others fell into the good soil, and it was giving fruit, coming up and increasing, and one bearing thirtyfold, and one sixty, and one a hundred.” <verse eid="MRK 4:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 4:9"/>And He was saying,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saying to them</char></note> <char style="wj">“He who has ears to hear, let him hear.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 4:9"/></para>

<para style="s">The Purpose of Jesus’ ParablesIsaiah 6:1–13</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 4:10"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:9–10</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 13:10–17</char></note>And when He was alone, those around Him with the Twelve were asking Him <char style="add">about</char> the parables.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">parable</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 4:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 4:11"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“To you⁺ has been given</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to know</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> the mystery of the kingdom of God, but to those who are outside, everything is done in parables, </char><verse eid="MRK 4:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 4:12"/><char style="wj">so that:</char> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 4:12">‘Seeing they might see and not perceive, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 4:12">and hearing they might hear and not understand, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 4:12">lest ever they might return, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 4:12">and they might be forgiven.’”” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 6:9–10 (see also LXX); BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">their sins</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 4:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Parable of the Sower ExplainedMatthew 13:18–23</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 4:13"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:11–15</char></note>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Do you⁺ not know this parable? And how will you⁺ know all the parables? </char><verse eid="MRK 4:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 4:14"/>The one sowing sows the word. <verse eid="MRK 4:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 4:15"/>Now these are the ones<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Some are like the seeds</char></note> along the path where the word is sown; and when they hear, immediately Satan comes and takes away the word sown in them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sown in their hearts</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 4:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 4:16"/>And these are likewise those sown upon the rocky <char style="add">places</char>, who, when they hear the word, immediately receive it with joy. <verse eid="MRK 4:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 4:17"/>And they have no root in themselves, but are temporary. Then, <char style="add">on</char> tribulation or persecution having come because of the word, immediately they are caused to stumble. <verse eid="MRK 4:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 4:18"/>And others are the ones sown among the thorns. These are the ones having heard the word, <verse eid="MRK 4:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 4:19"/>and the anxieties of the age, and the deceit of riches, and the desires concerning the other things, entering, choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful. <verse eid="MRK 4:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 4:20"/>And those are the ones having been sown upon the good soil, such as hear the word and receive <char style="add">it</char> and bear fruit: one thirtyfold, and one sixty, and one a hundred.” <verse eid="MRK 4:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Lesson of the LampLuke 8:16–18</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 4:21"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Does the lamp come so that it might be put under the basket or under the bed? Is it not so that it might be put upon the lampstand? </char><verse eid="MRK 4:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 4:22"/><char style="wj">For there is nothing that is hidden except so that it should be made manifest; nor was anything hidden away but so that it should come to be manifest. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 4:23"/>If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.” <verse eid="MRK 4:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 4:24"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Look at what you⁺ hear. In what measure you⁺ measure, it will be measured to you⁺, and it will be added to you⁺.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who hear</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="MRK 4:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 4:25"/><char style="wj">For whoever has, it will be given to him; and whoever does not have, even what he has will be taken away from him.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 4:25"/></para>

<para style="s">The Seed Growing Secretly</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 4:26"/>And He was saying, <char style="wj">“Thus is The kingdom of God: as a man may cast the seed upon the earth, </char><verse eid="MRK 4:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 4:27"/><char style="wj">and may sleep and rise night and day, and the seed may sprout and grow—he does not know how. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 4:28"/><char style="wj">Of itself,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For of itself</char></note><char style="wj"> the earth bears fruit—first a plant, then an ear, then full grain in the ear. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 4:29"/><char style="wj">And when the fruit may offer itself, immediately he sends the sickle, because the harvest has come.”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Joel 3:13, including LXX.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 4:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The Parable of the Mustard SeedMatthew 13:31–32</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 4:30"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 13:18–19</char></note>And He was saying, <char style="wj">“To what shall we liken the kingdom of God? Or in what parable shall we put</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">shall we compare</char></note><char style="wj"> it? </char><verse eid="MRK 4:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 4:31"/><char style="wj">It is like a grain of mustard, which, when it may be sown upon the earth, is smallest of all the seeds that are upon the earth. </char><verse eid="MRK 4:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 4:32"/><char style="wj">And when it may be sown, it comes up and becomes greater than all the garden plants and makes great branches, so that under its shadow the birds of the sky are able to lodge.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 4:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 4:33"/>And with many such parables He was speaking the word to them, as they were able to hear. <verse eid="MRK 4:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 4:34"/>And without a parable He was not speaking to them; but in private to His own disciples He was explaining all things. <verse eid="MRK 4:34"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Calms the StormPsalm 107:1–43</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 4:35"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:22–25</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 8:23–27</char></note>And on that day, evening having come, He says to them, <char style="wj">“Let us pass over to the other side.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 4:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 4:36"/>And having dismissed the crowd, they take Him along just as He was, in the boat; and other boats<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">other small boats</char></note> were with Him. <verse eid="MRK 4:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 4:37"/>And there comes a great storm of wind, and the waves were breaking into the boat, so as already to be filling the boat.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">so as already the boat was beginning to sink</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 4:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 4:38"/>And He was in the stern on the cushion, sleeping. And they awaken Him and say to Him, “Teacher, is it no concern to You that we are perishing?” <verse eid="MRK 4:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 4:39"/>And having been awoken, He rebuked the wind and said to the sea, <char style="wj">“Silence! Be still!”</char> And the wind abated, and there was a great calm. <verse eid="MRK 4:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 4:40"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“Why are you⁺ cowardly? Have you⁺</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How have you</char></note><char style="wj"> still no faith?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 4:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 4:41"/>And they feared <char style="add">with</char> great fear, and they were saying to one another, “Who then is this, that even the wind and the sea obey Him?” <verse eid="MRK 4:41"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="MRK 5"/>

<para style="s">The Demons and the Pigs</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 5:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:26–39</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 8:28–34</char></note>And they came to the other side of the sea, to the region of the Gerasenes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gadarenes</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Gergesenes</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 5:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 5:2"/>And <char style="add">on</char> His having gone out of the boat, immediately out of the tombs a man with an unclean spirit met Him, <verse eid="MRK 5:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 5:3"/>who had <char style="add">his</char> dwelling in the tombs. And no longer was anyone able<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">no one was able</char></note> to bind him, not even with a chain, <verse eid="MRK 5:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 5:4"/>because he often had been bound with shackles and chains, and the chains had been torn in two by him, and the shackles had been shattered. And no one had strength to subdue him. <verse eid="MRK 5:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 5:5"/>And constantly all night and day in the tombs and in the mountains<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the mountains and in the tombs</char></note> he was crying out and cutting himself with stones. <verse eid="MRK 5:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 5:6"/>And having seen Jesus from afar, he ran and fell on his knees before Him. <verse eid="MRK 5:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 5:7"/>And having cried out in a loud voice, he says, “What <char style="add">is it</char> to me and to You, Jesus, Son of the Most High God? I adjure You by God, do not torment me!” <verse eid="MRK 5:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 5:8"/>For He was saying to him, <char style="wj">“Come out of the man, unclean spirit!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 5:9"/>And He was asking him, <char style="wj">“What is your name?”</char> And he says to Him, “Legion <char style="add">is</char> my name, because we are many.” <verse eid="MRK 5:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 5:10"/>And he implored Him much that He might not send them out of the region. <verse eid="MRK 5:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 5:11"/>Now there was near the mountain a great herd of pigs feeding. <verse eid="MRK 5:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 5:12"/>And they implored Him,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And all the demons implored Him</char></note> saying, “Send us into the pigs, so that we may enter into them.” <verse eid="MRK 5:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 5:13"/>And He allowed them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And Jesus immediately allowed them</char></note> And the unclean spirits, having gone out, entered into the pigs, and the herd rushed down the steep bank into the sea—about two thousand—and they were drowned in the sea. <verse eid="MRK 5:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 5:14"/>And those feeding them<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Those feeding the pigs</char></note> fled and reported <char style="add">it</char> to the city and to the fields. And they went to see what it is that has happened. <verse eid="MRK 5:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 5:15"/>And they come to Jesus, and they see the <char style="add">man</char> possessed by demons sitting, clothed and sound-minded—the one having had the legion—and they were afraid. <verse eid="MRK 5:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 5:16"/>And those having seen <char style="add">it</char> related to them how it happened to the one possessed by demons, and about the pigs. <verse eid="MRK 5:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 5:17"/>And they began to implore Him to go away from their borders. <verse eid="MRK 5:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 5:18"/>And <char style="add">on</char> His having entered into the boat, the one having been possessed by demons was imploring Him that he might be with Him. <verse eid="MRK 5:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 5:19"/>And He did not permit him, but He says to him, <char style="wj">“Go to your house, to your⁺ own, and report to them how much the Lord has done for you, and how He had mercy on you.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 5:20"/>And he went away and began to proclaim in the Decapolis<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Ten Cities</char></note> how much Jesus did for him. And all were marveling. <verse eid="MRK 5:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Healing Touch of JesusMatthew 9:18–26</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 5:21"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 8:40–56</char></note>And <char style="add">on</char> Jesus having crossed over in the boat again to the other side, a great crowd was gathered to Him, and He was beside the sea. <verse eid="MRK 5:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 5:22"/>And<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">behold</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> one of the synagogue rulers comes, named Jairus, and having seen Him, he falls at His feet, <verse eid="MRK 5:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 5:23"/>and he implores Him much, saying, “My little daughter is holding at the end, so that, having come, You might lay the hands on her, so that she might be saved, and she might live.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saved, and she will live</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 5:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 5:24"/>And He went away with him. And a great crowd was following Him, and they were pressing in on Him. <verse eid="MRK 5:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 5:25"/>And a woman, being with a flow of blood twelve years, <verse eid="MRK 5:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 5:26"/>and having suffered much under many physicians, and having spent all of hers and having benefited in no way, but rather to the worse having come, <verse eid="MRK 5:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 5:27"/>having heard about Jesus, having come in the crowd behind, she touched His garment. <verse eid="MRK 5:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 5:28"/>For she was saying, “If I shall touch even His garments, I will be saved.” <verse eid="MRK 5:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 5:29"/>And immediately her flow of blood was dried up, and she knew in the body that she was healed from the affliction. <verse eid="MRK 5:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 5:30"/>And immediately Jesus, having known in Himself the power having gone out of Him, having turned in the crowd, said, <char style="wj">“Who touched My garments?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 5:31"/>And His disciples were saying to Him, “You see the crowd pressing in on You, and You say, <char style="wj">‘Who touched Me?’</char>” <verse eid="MRK 5:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 5:32"/>And He was looking around to see the one having done this. <verse eid="MRK 5:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 5:33"/>And the woman, having been afraid and trembling, knowing what had happened to her, came and fell down before Him, and told Him all the truth. <verse eid="MRK 5:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 5:34"/>And He said to her, <char style="wj">“Daughter, your faith has saved you; go in peace and be sound from your affliction.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 5:35"/><char style="add">In</char> His still speaking, they come from the synagogue ruler,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the house of the synagogue ruler</char></note> saying, “Your daughter died; why do you still trouble the Teacher?” <verse eid="MRK 5:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 5:36"/>But<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">immediately</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Jesus, having heard<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having ignored</char></note> the word spoken, says to the synagogue ruler, <char style="wj">“Do not fear; only believe.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 5:37"/>And He did not allow <char style="add">anyone</char> to follow with Him except Peter and James and John the brother of James. <verse eid="MRK 5:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 5:38"/>And they come<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He comes</char></note> to the house of the synagogue ruler, and He sees a commotion, and much weeping and wailing. <verse eid="MRK 5:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 5:39"/>And having entered, He says to them, <char style="wj">“Why do you⁺ make a commotion and weep? The child did not die, but sleeps.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 5:40"/>And they were laughing at Him. And He, having put all outside, takes along the father and the mother of the child, and those with Him, and He enters in where the child was.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">was lying</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 5:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 5:41"/>And having taken the hand of the child, He says to her, <char style="wj">“Talitha, koum!</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Talitha, cumi!</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> which is translated, <char style="wj">“Little girl, I say to you, arise!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 5:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 5:42"/>And immediately the girl arose and began walking, for she was of twelve years. And immediately<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">immediately</char></note> they were amazed with great amazement. <verse eid="MRK 5:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 5:43"/>And He instructed them much that no one should know this; and He said to be given to her to eat. <verse eid="MRK 5:43"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="MRK 6"/>

<para style="s">The Rejection at Nazareth</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 6:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 4:16–30</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 13:53–58</char></note>And He went out from there and came to His hometown, and His disciples follow Him. <verse eid="MRK 6:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 6:2"/>And <char style="add">on</char> the Sabbath having come, He began to teach in the synagogue; and many hearing were astonished, saying, “From where to this <char style="add">man</char> <char style="add">are</char> these things, and what <char style="add">is</char> the wisdom having been given to Him, and the miracles such as are done by His hands? <verse eid="MRK 6:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 6:3"/>Is not this the carpenter, the son of Mary, and brother of James and Joses and Judas and Simon? And are not His sisters here with us?” And they were taking offense at Him. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joses</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a variant of </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joseph</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 13:55.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 6:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 6:4"/>And Jesus was saying to them, <char style="wj">“A prophet is not without honor, except in his hometown and among his relatives and in his house.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 6:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 6:5"/>And He was not able to do there <char style="add">any</char> miracle except, having laid the hands on a few of the sick, He healed <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="MRK 6:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 6:6"/>And He marveled because of their unbelief. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 6:6">And He was going around the villages, teaching. <verse eid="MRK 6:6"/></para>

<para style="s">The Ministry of the TwelveMatthew 10:5–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 6:7"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:1–6</char></note>And He summons the Twelve, and He began to send them forth two <char style="add">by</char> two, and He was giving to them authority over the unclean spirits. <verse eid="MRK 6:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 6:8"/>And He instructed them that they may take nothing for the way, except only a staff—no bread, no bag,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">no bag, no bread</char></note> no copper<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">copper coins</char></note> in the belt— <verse eid="MRK 6:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 6:9"/>but to wear sandals, and you⁺ may not put on two tunics. <verse eid="MRK 6:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 6:10"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Wherever you⁺ may enter into a house, remain there until you⁺ may go out from there. </char><verse eid="MRK 6:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 6:11"/><char style="wj">And whatever place may not receive you⁺ nor hear you⁺, going out from there, shake off the dust that is under your⁺ feet, as a testimony against them.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Truly I say to you, it will be more tolerable for Sodom and Gomorrah in the day of judgment than for that city</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 10:15.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 6:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 6:12"/>And having gone out, they preached that they should repent. <verse eid="MRK 6:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 6:13"/>And they were casting out many demons, and they were anointing many sick with oil and healing <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="MRK 6:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Beheading of JohnMatthew 14:1–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 6:14"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:7–9</char></note>And King Herod heard; for His name became well known, And they were saying,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he was saying</char></note> “John, the one baptizing, has been raised out from the dead. And because of this, the miraculous powers are working in him.” <verse eid="MRK 6:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 6:15"/>But others were saying, “He is Elijah,” and others were saying, “A prophet, like one<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">or like one</char></note> of the prophets.” <verse eid="MRK 6:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 6:16"/>And having heard, Herod was saying, “John, whom I beheaded—this one was raised!”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“This is John, whom I beheaded; he has risen from the dead!”</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 6:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 6:17"/>For Herod himself, having sent, seized John and bound him in prison because of Herodias, the wife of Philip his brother, because he married her. <verse eid="MRK 6:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 6:18"/>For John was saying to Herod, “It is not lawful for you to have the wife of your brother.” <verse eid="MRK 6:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 6:19"/>And Herodias was holding it against him and was wanting to kill him, and she was not able. <verse eid="MRK 6:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 6:20"/>For Herod was afraid of John, knowing him <char style="add">as</char> a man righteous and holy, and he was keeping him safe. And having heard him, he was much perplexed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he did much</char></note> and heard him gladly. <verse eid="MRK 6:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 6:21"/>And an opportune day having come, when Herod on his birthday made a banquet to his great men, and to the commanders, and to the first <char style="add">men</char> of Galilee, <verse eid="MRK 6:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 6:22"/>and the daughter of Herodias<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some early manuscripts </char><char style="fq" closed="false">When his daughter Herodias</char></note> herself, having entered and having danced, pleased Herod and those reclining with <char style="add">him</char>. And the king said to the girl, “Ask me whatever you wish, and I will give <char style="add">it</char> to you.” <verse eid="MRK 6:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 6:23"/>And he swore to her much,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ, TR, and some CT do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">much</char></note> “Whatever, you might ask me, I will give to you, up to half of my kingdom!” <verse eid="MRK 6:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 6:24"/>And having gone out, she said to her mother, “What shall I ask?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 6:24">And she said, “The head of John, the one baptizing.” <verse eid="MRK 6:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 6:25"/>And having entered immediately with haste to the king, she asked, saying, “I want that at once you might give to me upon a platter the head of John the Baptist.” <verse eid="MRK 6:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 6:26"/>And the king, having been made very sorrowful because of the oaths and those reclining, did not want to set her aside. <verse eid="MRK 6:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 6:27"/>And immediately the king, having sent an executioner, commanded to be brought his head. And having gone away, he beheaded him in the prison <verse eid="MRK 6:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 6:28"/>and brought his head upon a platter and gave it to the girl, and the girl gave it to her mother. <verse eid="MRK 6:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 6:29"/>And having heard <char style="add">of it</char>, his disciples came and took up his body and laid it in a tomb. <verse eid="MRK 6:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The Feeding of the Five ThousandMatthew 14:13–21</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 6:30"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 6:1–15</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:10–17</char></note>And the apostles are gathered together to Jesus, and they reported to Him all things, as much as they did and as much as they taught. <verse eid="MRK 6:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 6:31"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“Come, you⁺ yourselves, apart to a wilderness place, and rest a little.”</char> For those coming and those going were many, and not even were they having opportunity to eat. <verse eid="MRK 6:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 6:32"/>And they went away in the boat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ECM, NA, SBL, WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a boat</char></note> to a wilderness place by themselves. <verse eid="MRK 6:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 6:33"/>And many saw them going and recognized,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">recognized Him</char></note> and they ran together there on foot from all the cities and went before them. <verse eid="MRK 6:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 6:34"/>And having gone out, He saw a great crowd and was moved with compassion toward them, because they were like sheep not having a shepherd. And He began to teach them many things. <verse eid="MRK 6:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 6:35"/>And the hour already being late, having come to Him, His disciples were saying, “The place is a wilderness, and the hour already <char style="add">is</char> late. <verse eid="MRK 6:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 6:36"/>Dismiss them so that, having gone to the surrounding fields and villages, they might buy for themselves something to eat.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">buy themselves food, for they have nothing to eat</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 6:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 6:37"/>But answering, He said to them, <char style="wj">“You⁺ give to them to eat.”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 6:37">And they say to Him, “Having gone away, shall we buy two hundred denarii<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see Matthew 20:2.</char></note> of loaves and give them to eat?” <verse eid="MRK 6:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 6:38"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“How many loaves do you⁺ have? Go, see.”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 6:38">And having known, they say, “Five, and two fish.” <verse eid="MRK 6:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 6:39"/>And He commanded them to make them all recline, groups <char style="add">by</char> groups, on the green grass. <verse eid="MRK 6:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 6:40"/>And they sat down groups <char style="add">by</char> groups, by hundreds and by fifties. <verse eid="MRK 6:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 6:41"/>And having taken the five loaves and the two fish, having looked up to the heaven, He blessed and broke the loaves. And He was giving <char style="add">them</char> to His disciples, so that they might set before them. And He divided the two fish among all. <verse eid="MRK 6:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 6:42"/>And all ate and were satisfied. <verse eid="MRK 6:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 6:43"/>And they took up twelve hand-baskets full of fragments, and of the fish. <verse eid="MRK 6:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 6:44"/>And those having eaten of the loaves were five thousand men.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">about five thousand men</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 6:44"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Walks on WaterMatthew 14:22–33</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 6:45"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 6:16–21</char></note>And immediately He compelled His disciples to enter into the boat and to go before <char style="add">Him</char> to the other side, to Bethsaida, until He dismisses the crowd. <verse eid="MRK 6:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="MRK 6:46"/>And having taken leave of them, He went away to the mountain to pray. <verse eid="MRK 6:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="MRK 6:47"/>And evening having come, the boat was in the midst of the sea, and He alone on the land. <verse eid="MRK 6:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="MRK 6:48"/>And having seen them straining in the rowing—for the wind was contrary to them—about the fourth watch of the night,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, between three and six in the morning</char></note> He goes to them, walking on the sea, and He was wanting to pass by them. <verse eid="MRK 6:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="MRK 6:49"/>And having seen Him walking on the sea, they thought that <char style="add">He</char> is a ghost, and they cried out. <verse eid="MRK 6:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="MRK 6:50"/>For all saw Him and were troubled. But immediately He spoke with them, and He says to them, <char style="wj">“Take courage! I am He! Do not be afraid.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 6:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="MRK 6:51"/>And He went up to them into the boat, and the wind abated. And exceedingly in abundance in themselves, they were amazed.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.51 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they were amazed beyond measure, and were marveling</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 6:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="MRK 6:52"/>For they did not understand about the loaves, but<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.52 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">because</char></note> their heart was hardened. <verse eid="MRK 6:52"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals at GennesaretMatthew 14:34–36</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="MRK 6:53"/>And having crossed over, they came to the land, to Gennesaret,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.53 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they came to the land of Gennesaret</char></note> and they drew to shore. <verse eid="MRK 6:53"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="MRK 6:54"/>And <char style="add">on</char> their having come out of the boat, immediately having recognized Him, <verse eid="MRK 6:54"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="MRK 6:55"/>they ran around all that region,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.55 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all that surrounding region</char></note> and they began to carry around on mats those being ill to where they were hearing that He is. <verse eid="MRK 6:55"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="MRK 6:56"/>And wherever He was entering into villages or into cities or into fields, they were laying the ailing in the marketplaces and were imploring Him that they might only touch the fringe of His garment. And as many as touched Him were saved. <verse eid="MRK 6:56"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="MRK 7"/>

<para style="s">The Tradition of the Elders</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 7:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 15:1–9</char></note>And the Pharisees and some of the scribes having come from Jerusalem are gathered together to Him. <verse eid="MRK 7:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 7:2"/>And they had seen some of His disciples, that with defiled hands—that is, unwashed—they are eating the loaves.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">(and) they found fault</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 7:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 7:3"/>(For the Pharisees and all the Jews do not eat unless they wash the hands to the fist,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">until they wash their hands ceremonially</char></note> holding to the tradition of the elders; <verse eid="MRK 7:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 7:4"/>and <char style="add">coming</char> from the marketplace, they do not eat unless they immerse; and there are many other things that they received to hold to—immersions of cups and pitchers and bronze vessels and couches.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">cups and vessels and bronze vessels.</char></note>) <verse eid="MRK 7:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 7:5"/>And the Pharisees and the scribes questioned Him, “Why do Your disciples not walk according to the tradition of the elders, but eat the bread with defiled<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">unwashed</char></note> hands?” <verse eid="MRK 7:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 7:6"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“Isaiah prophesied correctly about you⁺ hypocrites, as it has been written: </char></para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 7:6">‘This people honors Me with the lips, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 7:6">but their heart is kept far away from Me; <verse eid="MRK 7:6"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 7:7"/>and in vain they worship Me, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 7:7">teaching <char style="add">as</char> teachings the precepts of men.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 29:13 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="MRK 7:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 7:8"/>Having left the commandment of God, you⁺ hold to the tradition of men.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">—immersions of pitchers and cups; and you do many other things as such.</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 7:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 7:9"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Nobly do you⁺ set aside the commandment of God so that you⁺ might keep</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NA </char><char style="fq" closed="false">establish</char></note><char style="wj"> your⁺ tradition. </char><verse eid="MRK 7:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 7:10"/><char style="wj">For Moses said, ‘Honor your father and your mother,’ and, ‘The one speaking evil of father or mother, in death let him end.’</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 20:12; Deuteronomy 5:16</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 21:17; Leviticus 20:9</char></note><verse eid="MRK 7:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 7:11"/><char style="wj">But you⁺ say that if a man might say to the father or to the mother, ‘Whatever you might be profited from me is Corban’ (that is, a gift), </char><verse eid="MRK 7:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 7:12"/><char style="wj">no longer do you⁺ permit him to do anything for the father or for the mother, </char><verse eid="MRK 7:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 7:13"/><char style="wj">making void the word of God for your⁺ tradition, which you⁺ delivered. And you⁺ do many things as such.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 7:13"/></para>

<para style="s">What Defiles a ManMatthew 15:10–20</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 7:14"/>And having summoned the crowd<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all the crowd</char></note> again, He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Hear Me, all, and understand: </char><verse eid="MRK 7:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 7:15"/><char style="wj">There is nothing from outside the man entering into him that is able to defile him; but the things proceeding out of the man are the things defiling the man.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">16</char><char style="fq" closed="false">If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 7:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 7:17"/>And when He entered into the house from the crowd, His disciples were questioning Him <char style="add">about</char> the parable. <verse eid="MRK 7:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 7:18"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Thus are you⁺ also without understanding? Do you⁺ not understand that everything entering into the man from outside is not able to defile him, </char><verse eid="MRK 7:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 7:19"/><char style="wj">because it does not enter into his heart, but into the belly, and goes out into the sewer?”</char>—<char style="add">thus</char> purifying all the foods.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and then is eliminated, thereby expelling all foods.”</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 7:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 7:20"/>And He was saying, <char style="wj">“That which is proceeding out of the man, that defiles the man. </char><verse eid="MRK 7:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 7:21"/><char style="wj">For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil reasonings, sexual immorality, thefts, murders, adulteries,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some texts list these in a different order; some move </char><char style="fq" closed="false">adulteries</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> to verse 22.</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="MRK 7:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 7:22"/><char style="wj">covetous desires, wickednesses, deceit, sensuality, an evil eye, slander, pride, foolishness. </char><verse eid="MRK 7:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 7:23"/><char style="wj">All these evils proceed from within, and they defile the man.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 7:23"/></para>

<para style="s">The Faith of the Gentile WomanMatthew 15:21–28</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 7:24"/>And from there having risen up, He went away into the borders of Tyre.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH, BYZ, and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Sidon</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 15:21.</char></note> And having entered into a house, He was wanting no one to know <char style="add">it</char>, and He was not able to be hidden. <verse eid="MRK 7:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 7:25"/>But immediately, having heard<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For having heard</char></note> about Him, a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit, having come, fell at His feet. <verse eid="MRK 7:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 7:26"/>Now the woman was a Greek, Syrophoenician by race, and she was asking Him that He might cast the demon out of her daughter. <verse eid="MRK 7:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 7:27"/>And He was saying<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus was saying</char></note> to her, <char style="wj">“Permit the children first to be satisfied; for it is not good to take the bread of the children and to cast it to the dogs.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">puppies</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also verse 28</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 7:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 7:28"/>But she answered, and she says to Him, “Yes, Lord, even<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for even</char></note> the dogs under the table eat from the crumbs of the children.” <verse eid="MRK 7:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 7:29"/>And He said to her, <char style="wj">“Because of this word, go; the demon has gone forth out of your daughter.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 7:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 7:30"/>And having gone away to her house, she found the child laid on the bed, and the demon having gone out.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">she found the demon was gone, and her daughter was lying on the bed.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 7:30"/></para>

<para style="s">The Deaf and Mute ManMatthew 9:27–34</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 7:31"/>And again, having gone out from the borders of Tyre, He went through Sidon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Tyre and Sidon, He went</char></note> to the Sea of Galilee, through the midst of the borders of the Decapolis.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Ten Cities</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 7:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 7:32"/>And they bring to Him a deaf <char style="add">man</char> (and he spoke with difficulty), and they implore Him that He might lay the hand on him. <verse eid="MRK 7:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 7:33"/>And having taken him away from the crowd by himself, He put His fingers into his ears. And having spit, He touched his tongue. <verse eid="MRK 7:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 7:34"/>And having looked up to heaven, He sighed deeply, and He says to him, <char style="wj">“Ephphatha!”</char> (that is, <char style="wj">“Be opened!”</char>) <verse eid="MRK 7:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 7:35"/>And his ears were opened, and immediately<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, WH, TH, and SBL do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">immediately</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> the band of his tongue was loosed, and he was speaking rightly. <verse eid="MRK 7:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 7:36"/>And He instructed them that they should tell no one. But as much as He was instructing them, they were proclaiming <char style="add">it</char> more abundantly. <verse eid="MRK 7:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 7:37"/>And they were astonished above measure, saying, “He has done all things well! He makes both the deaf to hear and the mute to speak!” <verse eid="MRK 7:37"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="MRK 8"/>

<para style="s">The Feeding of the Four Thousand</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 8:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 15:29–39</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Kings 4:42–44</char></note>In those days, the crowd again<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">again</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> being great and not having what they might eat, having summoned the disciples,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His disciples</char></note> He says to them, <verse eid="MRK 8:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 8:2"/><char style="wj">“I have compassion toward the crowd, because already three days they continue with Me and have nothing that they might eat. </char><verse eid="MRK 8:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 8:3"/><char style="wj">And if I shall dismiss them hungry to their house, they will faint on the way. And</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For</char></note><char style="wj"> some of them have come from afar.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 8:4"/>And His disciples answered Him, “From where will anyone be able to satisfy these with loaves here in a wilderness?” <verse eid="MRK 8:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 8:5"/>And He was asking them, <char style="wj">“How many loaves do you⁺ have?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 8:5">And they said, “Seven.” <verse eid="MRK 8:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 8:6"/>And He commands the crowd to recline on the ground. And having taken the seven loaves, having given thanks, He broke <char style="add">them</char> and was giving <char style="add">them</char> to His disciples to set before <char style="add">them</char>. And they set <char style="add">them</char> before the crowd. <verse eid="MRK 8:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 8:7"/>And they had a few small fish. And having blessed them, He said to set before <char style="add">them</char> these also. <verse eid="MRK 8:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 8:8"/>And they ate and were satisfied, and they took up an abundance of fragments—seven baskets. <verse eid="MRK 8:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 8:9"/>And there were about four thousand.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">4,000 Men</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is implied here, that is, in addition to women and children; see Matthew 15:38; BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who had eaten</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> And He dismissed them. <verse eid="MRK 8:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 8:10"/>And immediately, having entered into the boat with His disciples, He went to the parts of Dalmanutha. <verse eid="MRK 8:10"/></para>

<para style="s">The Demand for a SignMatthew 16:1–4</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 8:11"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 12:54–56</char></note>And the Pharisees came out and began to dispute with Him, seeking from Him a sign from heaven, testing Him. <verse eid="MRK 8:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 8:12"/>And having sighed deeply in His spirit, He says, <char style="wj">“Why does this generation seek a sign? Truly I say to you⁺, no sign will be given to this generation.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 8:13"/>And having left them, having embarked again, He went away to the other side. <verse eid="MRK 8:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Leaven of the Pharisees and of HerodMatthew 16:5–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 8:14"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 12:1–3</char></note>And they forgot to take loaves, and except one loaf they had nothing with them in the boat. <verse eid="MRK 8:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 8:15"/>And He was instructing them, saying, <char style="wj">“Watch! Take heed of the leaven of the Pharisees and the leaven of Herod.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 8:16"/>And they were reasoning with one another because they had no loaves.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And they were reasoning with one another, saying, “It is because we have no bread.”</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 8:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 8:17"/>And having known, He says to them, <char style="wj">“Why do you⁺ reason that you⁺ have no loaves? Do you⁺ not yet perceive, nor do you⁺ understand? Do you⁺ have</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Do you still have</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> your⁺ heart hardened? </char><verse eid="MRK 8:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 8:18"/><char style="wj">‘Having eyes, do you⁺ not see? And having ears, do you⁺ not hear?’</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Deuteronomy 29:4, Isaiah 42:20, Jeremiah 5:21, and Ezekiel 12:2.</char></note><char style="wj"> And do you⁺ not remember? </char><verse eid="MRK 8:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 8:19"/><char style="wj">When I broke the five loaves for the five thousand, how many hand-baskets full of fragments did you⁺ take up?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 8:19">They say to Him, “Twelve.” <verse eid="MRK 8:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 8:20"/><char style="wj">“When also the seven were for the four thousand, how many baskets full of fragments did you⁺ take up?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 8:20">And they said, “Seven.” <verse eid="MRK 8:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 8:21"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Do you⁺ not yet understand?</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">How do you not yet understand?</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:21"/></para>

<para style="s">The Blind Man at Bethsaida</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 8:22"/>And they come<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He comes</char></note> to Bethsaida. And they bring to Him a blind <char style="add">man</char> and implore Him that He might touch him. <verse eid="MRK 8:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 8:23"/>And having taken hold of the hand of the blind <char style="add">man</char>, He led him forth outside of the village. And having spit upon his eyes, having laid the hands upon him, He was asking him, “Do you see anything?”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He was asking him if he could see anything.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 8:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 8:24"/>And having looked up, he was saying, “I see the men, because I see <char style="add">them</char> as trees walking.” <verse eid="MRK 8:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 8:25"/>Then He laid the hands upon his eyes again, and he opened his eyes, and he was restored,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">upon his eyes and made him look up, and his sight was restored</char></note> and he was seeing everything clearly. <verse eid="MRK 8:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 8:26"/>And He sent him to his house, saying, <char style="wj">“Do not enter into the village.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Do not enter into the village, nor tell anyone in the village.”</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 8:26"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter’s Confession of ChristMatthew 16:13–20</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 8:27"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 6:67–71</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:18–20</char></note>And Jesus and His disciples went out into the villages of Caesarea Philippi. And on the way, He was questioning His disciples, saying to them, <char style="wj">“Who do men say I am?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 8:28"/>And they spoke to Him, saying, “John the Baptist; and others, Elijah; and others, one of the prophets.” <verse eid="MRK 8:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 8:29"/>And He was questioning them, <char style="wj">“But you⁺, who do you⁺ say I am?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 8:29">Answering, Peter says to Him, “You are the Christ.” <verse eid="MRK 8:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 8:30"/>And He warned them that they should tell no one concerning Him. <verse eid="MRK 8:30"/></para>

<para style="s">Christ’s Passion ForetoldMatthew 16:21–23</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 8:31"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:21–22</char></note>And He began to teach them that it is necessary for the Son of Man to suffer many things, and to be rejected by the elders and the chief priests and the scribes, and to be killed, and after three days to rise again. <verse eid="MRK 8:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 8:32"/>And He was speaking openly the word. And Peter, having taken Him aside, began to rebuke Him. <verse eid="MRK 8:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 8:33"/>But having turned and having seen His disciples, He rebuked Peter, and He says, <char style="wj">“Get behind Me, Satan, because you do not have in mind the things of God, but the things of men.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:33"/></para>

<para style="s">Take Up Your CrossMatthew 16:24–28</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 8:34"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:23–27</char></note>And having summoned the crowd with His disciples, He said to them, <char style="wj">“If anyone wants to come after</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">follow after</char></note><char style="wj"> Me, let him deny himself and take up his cross and follow Me. </char><verse eid="MRK 8:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 8:35"/><char style="wj">For whoever may want to save his life will lose it, but whoever will lose his life on account of Me and of the gospel, he will save it.</char> <verse eid="MRK 8:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 8:36"/>For what does it profit a man to gain the whole world and to lose his soul?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">What does it profit a man if he gains the whole world yet forfeits his soul?</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 8:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 8:37"/>For<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Or</char></note> what shall a man give <char style="add">as</char> an exchange for his soul? <verse eid="MRK 8:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 8:38"/>For whoever may be ashamed of Me and My words in this adulterous and sinful generation, the Son of Man also will be ashamed of him when He shall come in the glory of His Father with the holy angels.” <verse eid="MRK 8:38"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="MRK 9"/>

<para style="s">The Transfiguration</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 9:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Peter 1:16–21</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:28–36</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 17:1–13</char></note>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Truly I say to you⁺ that there are some of those standing here who shall not taste of death until they shall see the kingdom of God having come in power.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 9:2"/>And after six days, Jesus takes along Peter and James and John, and He brings them up onto a high mountain by themselves alone. And He was transfigured before them, <verse eid="MRK 9:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 9:3"/>and His garments became radiant, exceedingly white,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as snow</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> such as no launderer on the earth is able thus to whiten <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="MRK 9:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 9:4"/>And there appeared to them Elijah with Moses, and they were talking with Jesus. <verse eid="MRK 9:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 9:5"/>And answering, Peter says to Jesus, “Rabbi, it is good for us to be here. And let us make three tabernacles<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">three shelters</char></note>—one for You, and one for Moses, and one for Elijah.” <verse eid="MRK 9:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 9:6"/>For he did not know what he should answer, for they were terrified. <verse eid="MRK 9:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 9:7"/>And there was a cloud overshadowing them, and there was a voice out of the cloud: “This is My Son, the Beloved; listen to Him!” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR and GOC include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saying</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 9:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 9:8"/>And suddenly, having looked around, no longer did they see <char style="add">anyone</char> but Jesus alone with themselves. <verse eid="MRK 9:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 9:9"/>And <char style="add">in</char> their coming down from the mountain, He instructed them that they should relate to no one what they saw, except when the Son of Man should rise out from the dead. <verse eid="MRK 9:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 9:10"/>And they kept the word to themselves, discussing what it is to rise out from the dead. <verse eid="MRK 9:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 9:11"/>And they were questioning Him, saying, “The scribes say that it is necessary for Elijah to come first.” <verse eid="MRK 9:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 9:12"/>And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Elijah indeed, having come first, restores all things. And how has it been written about the Son of Man that He should suffer many things and be set at nothing? </char><verse eid="MRK 9:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 9:13"/><char style="wj">But I say to you⁺ that Elijah has also come, and they did to him whatever they were wanting, as it has been written of him.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Boy with an Evil SpiritMatthew 17:14–18</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 9:14"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:37–42</char></note>And having come to the disciples, they saw<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He saw</char></note> a great crowd around them, and scribes disputing with them. <verse eid="MRK 9:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 9:15"/>And immediately all the crowd, having seen Him, were greatly amazed, and running to <char style="add">Him</char>, they were greeting Him. <verse eid="MRK 9:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 9:16"/>And He questioned them,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He questioned the scribes</char></note> <char style="wj">“What are you⁺ disputing with them?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 9:17"/>And one out of the crowd answered Him, “Teacher, I brought to You my son, having a mute spirit. <verse eid="MRK 9:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 9:18"/>And wherever it might seize him, it throws him down, and he foams and gnashes his teeth and is withering away.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and becomes rigid</char></note> And I spoke to Your disciples that they might cast it out, and they did not have the strength.” <verse eid="MRK 9:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 9:19"/>And answering them, He says, <char style="wj">“O unbelieving generation, until when will I be with you⁺? Until when will I bear with you⁺? Bring him to Me.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 9:20"/>And they brought him to Him, and having seen Him, the spirit immediately threw him into convulsions. And having fallen upon the ground, he was rolling around, foaming. <verse eid="MRK 9:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 9:21"/>And He questioned his father, <char style="wj">“How long a time is it that this has been with him?”</char> And he said, “From childhood.” <verse eid="MRK 9:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 9:22"/>And often it also cast him into the fire and into the waters, so that it might destroy him. But if You are able <char style="add">to do</char> anything, help us, having compassion on us.” <verse eid="MRK 9:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 9:23"/>And Jesus said to him, <char style="wj">“‘If You are able’?</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“If you are able to believe!</char></note><char style="wj"> All things are possible to the one believing!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 9:24"/>Immediately, having cried out,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having cried out with tears</char></note> the father of the child was saying, “I believe;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Lord, I believe</char></note> help my unbelief!” <verse eid="MRK 9:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 9:25"/>And Jesus, having seen that a crowd is running together, rebuked the unclean spirit, saying to it, <char style="wj">“Mute and deaf</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some translators </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Deaf and mute</char></note><char style="wj"> spirit, I command you, come out of him, and no more may you enter into him.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 9:26"/>And having cried out, and having thrown him into many convulsions, it came out. And he became as if dead, so as for many to say that he was dead. <verse eid="MRK 9:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 9:27"/>But Jesus, having taken him by the hand, raised him up, and he arose. <verse eid="MRK 9:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 9:28"/>And <char style="add">on</char> His having entered into the house, His disciples were questioning Him by Himself, “Why were we not able to cast it out?” <verse eid="MRK 9:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 9:29"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“This kind is able to come out by nothing except by prayer.”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">prayer and fasting</char></note><verse eid="MRK 9:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The Second Prediction of the PassionMatthew 17:22–23</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 9:30"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:43–45</char></note>Having gone out from there, they were passing through Galilee. And He did not wish that anyone should know, <verse eid="MRK 9:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 9:31"/>for He was teaching His disciples. And He was saying to them, <char style="wj">“The Son of Man is delivered into the hands of men, and they will kill Him; and having been killed, after three days</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on the third day</char></note><char style="wj"> He will rise.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 9:32"/>But they were not understanding the saying, and they were afraid to question Him. <verse eid="MRK 9:32"/></para>

<para style="s">The Greatest in the KingdomMatthew 18:1–5</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 9:33"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 9:46–50</char></note>And they came<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he came</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to Capernaum. And being in the house, He was questioning them, <char style="wj">“What were you⁺ reasoning</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">among yourselves</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> on the way?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 9:34"/>But they were silent, for they discussed with one another on the way who <char style="add">was</char> greater. <verse eid="MRK 9:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 9:35"/>And having sat down, He called the Twelve, and He says to them, <char style="wj">“If anyone wants to be first, he will be last of all and servant of all.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 9:36"/>And having taken a little child, He set him in their midst. And having taken him in <char style="add">His</char> arms, He said to them, <verse eid="MRK 9:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 9:37"/><char style="wj">“Whoever shall receive one of such little children in My name receives Me; and whoever shall receive Me does not receive Me but the One having sent Me.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 9:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 9:38"/>John said to Him, “Teacher, we saw someone casting out demons in Your name who does not follow us, and we were forbidding him, because he was not following us.” <verse eid="MRK 9:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 9:39"/>And Jesus said, <char style="wj">“Do not forbid him. For there is no one who will do a mighty work in My name and will be able quickly to speak evil of Me. </char><verse eid="MRK 9:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 9:40"/><char style="wj">For whoever is not against us is for us.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and Stephanus TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">not against you is for you</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="MRK 9:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 9:41"/><char style="wj">For whoever shall give you⁺ to drink a cup of water because you⁺ are Christ’s in name,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a cup of water in My name because you are Christ’s</char></note><char style="wj"> truly I say to you⁺ that he shall never lose his reward. </char><verse eid="MRK 9:41"/></para>

<para style="s">Temptations and TrespassesMatthew 18:6–9</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 9:42"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 17:1–4</char></note>And whoever might cause to stumble one of these little ones believing in Me, it is better for him rather if a heavy millstone<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a millstone</char></note> is put around his neck and he has been cast into the sea. <verse eid="MRK 9:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 9:43"/>And if your hand may cause you to stumble, cut it off; it is better for you to enter into life crippled than, having two hands, to go away into Gehenna,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">hell</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 45 and 47</char></note> into the unquenchable fire.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">44</char><char style="fq" closed="false">where ‘their worm does not die, and the fire is not quenched’</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see verse 48 and Isaiah 66:24.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 9:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 9:45"/>And if your foot may cause you to stumble, cut it off. It is better for you to enter into life lame than, having the two feet, to be cast into Gehenna.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.45 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">46</char><char style="fq" closed="false">where ‘their worm does not die, and the fire is not quenched’</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see verse 48 and Isaiah 66:24.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 9:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="MRK 9:47"/>And if your eye may cause you to stumble, cast it out. It is better for you to enter into the kingdom of God one-eyed than, having two eyes, to be cast<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and go away</char></note> into Gehenna,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">into the gehenna of fire</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 9:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="MRK 9:48"/>where ‘their worm does not die, and the fire is not quenched.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the worm</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 66:24</char></note><verse eid="MRK 9:48"/></para>

<para style="s">Good SaltMatthew 5:13–16</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="MRK 9:49"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 14:34–35</char></note>For everyone will be salted with fire.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and every sacrifice will be salted with salt</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 9:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="MRK 9:50"/>The salt <char style="add">is</char> good, but if the salt should become unsalty, with what will you⁺ season it? Have salt among yourselves, and be at peace with one another.” <verse eid="MRK 9:50"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="MRK 10"/>

<para style="s">Teachings about Divorce</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 10:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 19:1–12</char></note>And from there, having risen up, He comes into the borders of Judea, and beyond the Jordan. And again crowds come together to Him, and as He had been accustomed, again He was teaching them. <verse eid="MRK 10:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 10:2"/>And having come, the Pharisees were questioning Him whether it is lawful for a husband to send away a wife—testing Him. <verse eid="MRK 10:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 10:3"/>And answering, He said to them, <char style="wj">“What did Moses command you⁺?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 10:4"/>And they said, “Moses allowed <char style="add">us</char> to write a roll of divorce and to send <char style="add">her</char> away.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Deuteronomy 24:1.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 10:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 10:5"/>But Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“For your⁺ hardness of heart he wrote you⁺ this commandment; </char><verse eid="MRK 10:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 10:6"/><char style="wj">but from the beginning of creation, ‘He made them male and female.’ </char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 1:27; Genesis 5:2</char></note><verse eid="MRK 10:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 10:7"/><char style="wj">‘On account of this a man will leave his father and mother and be joined to his wife, </char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE and WH do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and be joined to his wife.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 10:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 10:8"/><char style="wj">and the two will be for one flesh,’</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 2:24 (see also LXX)</char></note><char style="wj"> so that they are no longer two, but one flesh. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 10:9"/><char style="wj">Therefore what God has yoked together, let man not separate.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 10:10"/>And in the house again, the disciples<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His disciples</char></note> were questioning Him about this. <verse eid="MRK 10:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 10:11"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Whoever shall send away his wife and shall marry another, he commits adultery against her. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 10:12"/><char style="wj">And if a woman, having divorced her husband, shall marry another, she commits adultery.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Blesses the ChildrenMatthew 19:13–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 10:13"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 18:15–17</char></note>And they were bringing little children to Him so that He might touch them, but the disciples rebuked them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">rebuked those who brought them</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 10:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 10:14"/>And having seen, Jesus was indignant and said to them, <char style="wj">“Permit the little children to come to Me; do not forbid them! For of such is the kingdom of God. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 10:15"/><char style="wj">Truly I say to you⁺, whoever shall not receive the kingdom of God as a little child shall never enter into it.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 10:16"/>And having taken <char style="add">them</char> in <char style="add">His</char> arms, He was blessing them, having laid the hands on them. <verse eid="MRK 10:16"/></para>

<para style="s">The Rich Young ManMatthew 19:16–30</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 10:17"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 18:18–30</char></note>And of Him going forth into the way, one<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">someone</char></note> having run up and having knelt down to Him was questioning Him, “Good Teacher, what shall I do so that I may inherit eternal life?” <verse eid="MRK 10:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 10:18"/>And Jesus said to him, <char style="wj">“Why do you call Me good? No one is good except one—God. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 10:19"/><char style="wj">You know the commandments: ‘You shall not murder, you shall not commit adultery, you shall not steal, you shall not bear false witness, you shall not defraud, honor your father and mother.”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You shall not commit adultery, you shall not murder</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 20:12–16; Deuteronomy 5:16–20</char></note><verse eid="MRK 10:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 10:20"/>And he was saying to Him, “Teacher, all these I kept from my youth.” <verse eid="MRK 10:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 10:21"/>And Jesus, having looked on him, loved him and said to him, <char style="wj">“One thing to you is lacking: Go,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">If you wish to be perfect, go</char></note><char style="wj"> sell as much as you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow Me.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and come, take up the cross, and follow Me.</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 10:22"/>And having been sad at the word, he went away grieving; for he was one having many possessions. <verse eid="MRK 10:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 10:23"/>And having looked around, Jesus says to His disciples, <char style="wj">“How difficultly those having riches will enter into the kingdom of God!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 10:24"/>And the disciples were astonished at His words. But Jesus, answering, says to them again, <char style="wj">“Children, how difficult it is to enter</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">how difficult it is for those who trust in riches to enter</char></note><char style="wj"> into the kingdom of God! </char><verse eid="MRK 10:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 10:25"/><char style="wj">It is</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For it is</char></note><char style="wj"> easier for a camel to pass through the eye of the needle than for a rich man to enter into the kingdom of God.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 10:26"/>And they were exceedingly astonished, saying among themselves,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saying to Him</char></note> “And who is able to be saved?” <verse eid="MRK 10:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 10:27"/>Having looked on them, Jesus says, <char style="wj">“With men it is impossible, but not with God; for all things are possible with God.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 10:28"/>Peter began to say to Him, “Behold, we left all and followed You.” <verse eid="MRK 10:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 10:29"/>Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Jesus</char></note> was saying, <char style="wj">“Truly I say to you⁺, there is no one who left house or brothers or sisters or mother or father</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">or wife</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> or children or fields for My sake and for the sake of the gospel </char><verse eid="MRK 10:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 10:30"/><char style="wj">who shall not receive a hundredfold now in this time—houses and brothers and sisters</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC and F35 include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and fathers</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> and mothers and children and fields, with persecutions—and in the age that is coming, eternal life. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 10:31"/><char style="wj">But many first will be last, and the last, first.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:31"/></para>

<para style="s">The Third Prediction of the PassionMatthew 20:17–19</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 10:32"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 18:31–34</char></note>And they were on the way, going up to Jerusalem, and Jesus was going on before them. And they were astonished, and those following were afraid.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as they followed, they were afraid</char></note> And having taken aside the Twelve again, He began to tell them the things being about to happen to Him: <verse eid="MRK 10:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 10:33"/><char style="wj">“Behold, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be betrayed to the chief priests and to the scribes, and they will condemn Him to death and will betray Him to the Gentiles. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 10:34"/><char style="wj">And they will mock Him and will spit upon Him and will flog Him</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will mock Him and will flog Him and will spit upon Him</char></note><char style="wj"> and will kill Him, and after three days</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on the third day</char></note><char style="wj"> He will rise again.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:34"/></para>

<para style="s">The Request of James and JohnMatthew 20:20–28</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 10:35"/>And James and John, the sons of Zebedee, come to Him, saying to Him, “Teacher, we wish that You would do for us whatever we might ask You.” <verse eid="MRK 10:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 10:36"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“What do you⁺ want Me to do for you⁺?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 10:37"/>And they said to Him, “Give to us that one at Your right hand and one at <char style="add">Your</char> left hand we might sit in Your glory.” <verse eid="MRK 10:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 10:38"/>And Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“You⁺ do not know what you⁺ ask. Are you⁺ able to drink the cup that I drink, or</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and</char></note><char style="wj"> to be baptized with the baptism with which I am baptized?”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 10:39"/>And they said to Him, “We are able.” And Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“You⁺ will drink</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You will indeed drink</char></note><char style="wj"> the cup that I drink, and you⁺ will be baptized with the baptism with which I am baptized. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 10:40"/><char style="wj">But to sit at My right hand or</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and</char></note><char style="wj"> at My left hand is not Mine to give, but it is to those for whom it has been prepared.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 10:41"/>And having heard, the ten began to be indignant about James and John. <verse eid="MRK 10:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 10:42"/>And Jesus, having summoned them, says to them, <char style="wj">“You⁺ know that those considered to rule over the Gentiles exercise lordship over them, and their great ones exercise authority over them. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 10:43"/><char style="wj">But it is not</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">it shall not be</char></note><char style="wj"> thus among you⁺. But whoever may want to become great among you⁺, he will be your⁺ servant; </char><verse eid="MRK 10:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 10:44"/><char style="wj">and whoever may want to be first among you⁺, he will be slave of all. </char><verse eid="MRK 10:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 10:45"/><char style="wj">For even the Son of Man did not come to be served, but to serve, and to give His life as a ransom for many.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 10:45"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Heals BartimaeusMatthew 20:29–34</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="MRK 10:46"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 18:35–43</char></note>And they come to Jericho. And <char style="add">in</char> His going out from Jericho—and His disciples and a large crowd—the son of Timaeus, Bartimaeus, a blind beggar, was sitting beside the road.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.46 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Bartimaeus, a blind one, was sitting beside the road begging</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 10:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="MRK 10:47"/>And having heard that it is Jesus of Nazareth, he began to cry out and to say, “Jesus, Son of David, have mercy on me!” <verse eid="MRK 10:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="MRK 10:48"/>And many were rebuking him that he should be silent. But much more he was crying out, “Son of David, have mercy on me!” <verse eid="MRK 10:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="MRK 10:49"/>And having stood, Jesus said, <char style="wj">“Call him.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus asked for him to be called over</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 10:49">And they call the blind <char style="add">man</char>, saying to him, “Take courage! Rise up! He calls you.” <verse eid="MRK 10:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="MRK 10:50"/>And having cast away his cloak, having leaped up,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.50 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having risen up</char></note> he came to Jesus. <verse eid="MRK 10:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="MRK 10:51"/>And answering him, Jesus says, <char style="wj">“What do you desire that I may do for you?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 10:51">And the blind <char style="add">man</char> said to Him, “Rabboni, that I may receive sight.” <verse eid="MRK 10:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="MRK 10:52"/>“And” Jesus said to him, <char style="wj">“Go, your faith has saved you.”</char> And immediately he received his sight, and he was following Him on the road. <verse eid="MRK 10:52"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="MRK 11"/>

<para style="s">The Triumphal Entry</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 11:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 12:12–19</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 19:28–40</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 21:1–11</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Zechariah 9:9–13</char></note>And when they draw near to Jerusalem, to Bethphage<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Most MT </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Bethsphage</char></note> and Bethany, toward the Mount of Olives, He sends two of His disciples, <verse eid="MRK 11:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 11:2"/>and He says to them, <char style="wj">“Go into the village ahead of you⁺, and immediately entering into it you⁺ will find a colt tied, on which no one of men yet sat.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">has sat</char></note><char style="wj"> Having loosed it, also bring it. </char><verse eid="MRK 11:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 11:3"/><char style="wj">And if anyone should say to you⁺, ‘Why are you⁺ doing this?’ say, ‘Because the Lord has need of it, and immediately He sends it again here.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He sends it here</char></note><char style="wj">’”</char> <verse eid="MRK 11:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 11:4"/>And they went away and found a colt<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, F35, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the colt</char></note> tied at the door outside on the street, and they loose it. <verse eid="MRK 11:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 11:5"/>And some of those standing there were saying to them, “What are you⁺ doing, loosing the colt?” <verse eid="MRK 11:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 11:6"/>And they said to them just as Jesus said,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">commanded</char></note> and they allowed them. <verse eid="MRK 11:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 11:7"/>And they bring the colt to Jesus, and they cast on it their garments, and He sat on it. <verse eid="MRK 11:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 11:8"/>And many spread their garments in the road, and others, branches having been cut from the fields.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and they spread them on the road</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 11:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 11:9"/>And those going before and those following were crying out: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 11:9">“Hosanna!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 11:9">“Blessed is the One coming in the name of the Lord!”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hosanna</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a transliteration of the Hebrew </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Hosia-na</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, meaning </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Save, we pray</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Save now</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, which became a shout of praise; see Psalm 118:25.</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 118:26</char></note><verse eid="MRK 11:9"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 11:10"/>“Blessed <char style="add">is</char> the coming kingdom of our father David!” </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 11:10">“Hosanna in the highest!”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Blessed is the kingdom of our father David coming in the name of the Lord!”</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Hosanna in the highest heaven!”</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Psalm 118:25 and Psalm 148:1.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 11:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 11:11"/>And He entered into Jerusalem, into the temple.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 15, 16, and 27</char></note> And having looked around at all things, the hour being already late, He went out to Bethany with the Twelve. <verse eid="MRK 11:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Curses the Fig TreeMatthew 21:18–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 11:12"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Mark 11:20–25</char></note>And on the next day, <char style="add">on</char> their having gone out from Bethany, He was hungry. <verse eid="MRK 11:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 11:13"/>And having seen a fig tree from afar having leaves, He went <char style="add">to see</char> if perhaps He will find anything on it. And having gone to it, He found nothing except leaves, for it was not the season of figs. <verse eid="MRK 11:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 11:14"/>And answering, He said<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Jesus said</char></note> to it, <char style="wj">“No more to the age may anyone eat of your fruit.”</char> And His disciples were hearing. <verse eid="MRK 11:14"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Cleanses the TempleMatthew 21:12–17</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 11:15"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 2:12–25</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 19:45–48</char></note>And they come to Jerusalem. And having entered into the temple, He began to cast out those selling and those buying in the temple. And He overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those selling the doves, <verse eid="MRK 11:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 11:16"/>and He was not permitting that anyone might carry a vessel through the temple. <verse eid="MRK 11:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 11:17"/>And He was teaching and was saying to them, <char style="wj">“Has it not been written: ‘My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations’? But you⁺ have made it ‘a den of robbers.’</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 56:7</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Jeremiah 7:11</char></note><verse eid="MRK 11:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 11:18"/>And the chief priests and the scribes<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">scribes and chief priests</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">scribes, Pharisees, and chief priests</char></note> heard, and they were seeking how they might destroy Him. For they were afraid of Him, for all the crowd was astonished at His teaching. <verse eid="MRK 11:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 11:19"/>And when evening came, they were going forth<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He was going forth</char></note> out of the city. <verse eid="MRK 11:19"/></para>

<para style="s">The Withered Fig TreeMatthew 21:18–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 11:20"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Mark 11:12–14</char></note>And passing by in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered from the roots. <verse eid="MRK 11:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 11:21"/>And having remembered, Peter says to Him, “Rabbi, look, the fig tree that You cursed has withered.” <verse eid="MRK 11:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 11:22"/>And answering, Jesus says to them, <char style="wj">“Have faith from God. </char><verse eid="MRK 11:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 11:23"/><char style="wj">Truly</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For truly</char></note><char style="wj"> I say to you⁺ that whoever shall say to this mountain, ‘Be taken away and be cast into the sea,’ and shall not doubt in his heart but shall believe that what he says happens, it will be done for him.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">whatever he says will be done for him</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="MRK 11:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 11:24"/><char style="wj">Because of this, I say to you⁺, all things—as many as you⁺ pray and ask—believe that you⁺ receive, and it will be unto you⁺. </char><verse eid="MRK 11:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 11:25"/>And when you⁺ stand praying, if you⁺ have anything against anyone, forgive, so that your⁺ Father who <char style="add">is</char> in the heavens may also forgive you⁺ your⁺ trespasses.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">26</char><char style="fq" closed="false">But if you do not forgive, neither will your Father in heaven forgive your trespasses</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 6:15.</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 11:25"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus’ Authority ChallengedMatthew 21:23–27</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 11:27"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 20:1–8</char></note>And they come again to Jerusalem, and <char style="add">in</char> His walking in the temple, the chief priests and the scribes and the elders come to Him. <verse eid="MRK 11:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 11:28"/>And they were saying to Him, “By what authority do You do these things? Or<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And</char></note> who gave You this authority, that You should do these things?” <verse eid="MRK 11:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 11:29"/>And Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“I will question you⁺ one word, and you⁺ shall answer Me, and I will tell you⁺ by what authority I do these things. </char><verse eid="MRK 11:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 11:30"/><char style="wj">The baptism of John—was it from heaven or from men? Answer Me!</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Answer Me!</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <verse eid="MRK 11:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 11:31"/>And they were reasoning with themselves, saying, “What should we say?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">What should we say?</char></note> If we should say, ‘From heaven,’ He will say, ‘Why then did you⁺ not believe him?’ <verse eid="MRK 11:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 11:32"/>But should we say, ‘From men’...” they were afraid of the crowd, for all were holding that John truly was a prophet. <verse eid="MRK 11:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 11:33"/>And answering Jesus, they say, “We do not know.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 11:33">And Jesus says to them, <char style="wj">“Neither do I tell you⁺ by what authority I do these things.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 11:33"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="MRK 12"/>

<para style="s">The Parable of the Wicked Tenants</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 12:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 20:9–18</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 21:33–46</char></note>And He began to speak to them in parables: <char style="wj">“A man planted a vineyard, and he placed around it a fence and dug a wine vat and built a tower, and he rented it out to farmers and traveled abroad. </char><verse eid="MRK 12:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 12:2"/>And he sent a servant to the farmers in the season, so that he might receive from the farmers from the fruit of the vineyard. <verse eid="MRK 12:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 12:3"/>And having taken him, they beat <char style="add">him</char> and sent <char style="add">him</char> away empty. <verse eid="MRK 12:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 12:4"/>And again he sent to them another servant, and that one<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">casting stones</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> they struck on the head and dishonored <char style="add">him</char>.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and sent him away</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 12:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 12:5"/>And he sent another, and that one they killed—and many others—indeed beating some and killing some. <verse eid="MRK 12:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 12:6"/>Yet having one<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">his one</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> beloved son, he sent him to them last, saying, ‘They will respect my son.’ <verse eid="MRK 12:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 12:7"/>But those farmers said<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">But when the farmers saw him coming, they said</char></note> to themselves, ‘This is the heir; come, let us kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.’ <verse eid="MRK 12:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 12:8"/>And having taken <char style="add">him</char>, they killed him and cast him out of the vineyard. <verse eid="MRK 12:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 12:9"/>What therefore<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL and WH do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">therefore</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> will the lord of the vineyard do? He will come and will destroy the farmers, and he will give the vineyard to others. <verse eid="MRK 12:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 12:10"/>Did you⁺ not even read this Scripture: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 12:10">‘The stone that those building rejected, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 12:10">this became the head of the corner; <verse eid="MRK 12:10"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 12:11"/>this was from the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 12:11">and it is marvelous in our eyes’?” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 118:22–23</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 12:12"/>And they were seeking<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the leaders sought</char></note> to lay hold of Him, and they feared the crowd; for they knew that He spoke the parable against them. And having left Him, they went away. <verse eid="MRK 12:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Paying Taxes to CaesarMatthew 22:15–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 12:13"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 20:19–26</char></note>And they send to Him some of the Pharisees and Herodians, so that they might catch Him in a word. <verse eid="MRK 12:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 12:14"/>And having come, they say to Him, “Teacher, we know that You are true, and to You there is no care about <char style="add">anyone</char>; for You do not look to the appearance of men, but You teach the way of God on the basis of truth. Is it lawful<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Tell us then, is it lawful</char></note> to give tribute to Caesar or not? Should we pay or not pay?” <verse eid="MRK 12:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 12:15"/>But knowing their hypocrisy, He said to them, <char style="wj">“Why do you⁺ test Me? Bring Me a denarius,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see Matthew 20:2.</char></note><char style="wj"> so that I might see it.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 12:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 12:16"/>And they brought <char style="add">it</char>. And He says to them, <char style="wj">“Whose image is this—and the inscription?”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 12:16">And they said to Him, “Caesar’s.” <verse eid="MRK 12:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 12:17"/>And<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">answering</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Jesus said to them, <char style="wj">“Give back the things of Caesar to Caesar, and the things of God to God.”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 12:17">And they were marveling at Him. <verse eid="MRK 12:17"/></para>

<para style="s">The Sadducees and the ResurrectionMatthew 22:23–33</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 12:18"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 20:27–40</char></note>And <char style="add">some</char> Sadducees, who say there is not a resurrection, come to Him. And they were questioning Him, saying, <verse eid="MRK 12:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 12:19"/>“Teacher, Moses wrote for us that if anyone’s brother should die and leave behind a wife and not leave a child, that his brother should take the wife and should raise up seed for his brother. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 25:5</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 12:20"/>There were seven brothers; and the first took a wife, and dying, left no seed. <verse eid="MRK 12:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 12:21"/>And the second took her and died, not having left behind seed; and the third likewise. <verse eid="MRK 12:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 12:22"/>And the seven<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">who had her</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> left no seed. Last of all, the woman also died. <verse eid="MRK 12:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 12:23"/>In the resurrection, when they rise,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">In the resurrection, then,</char></note> of which of them will she be wife? For the seven had her <char style="add">as</char> wife.” <verse eid="MRK 12:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 12:24"/>Jesus was saying to them,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And Jesus answered them</char></note> <char style="wj">“Do you⁺ not go astray because of this, not knowing the Scriptures, nor the power of God? </char><verse eid="MRK 12:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 12:25"/><char style="wj">For when they rise out from the dead, they neither marry nor are given in marriage; but they are like angels in the heavens. </char><verse eid="MRK 12:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 12:26"/>But concerning the dead, that they rise, did you⁺ not read in the book of Moses, at the bush, how God spoke to him, saying, ‘I <char style="add">am</char> the God of Abraham and the God of Isaac and the God of Jacob’? <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 3:6</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 12:27"/>He is not God of the dead, but<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> of the living. You⁺ go astray<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Therefore you go astray</char></note> greatly!” <verse eid="MRK 12:27"/></para>

<para style="s">The Greatest CommandmentDeuteronomy 6:1–19</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 12:28"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 22:34–40</char></note>And one of the scribes having come, having heard them reasoning together, having seen that He answered them well, questioned Him, “Which commandment is first of all?” <verse eid="MRK 12:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 12:29"/>Jesus answered, <char style="wj">“The first is, ‘Hear, O Israel: The Lord our God, the Lord is One. </char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of all the commandments</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 12:30"/><char style="wj">And you shall love the Lord your God out of all your heart and out of all your soul and out of all your mind and out of all your strength.’ </char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 6:4–5; BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">This is the first commandment</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 12:31"/><char style="wj">The second is this: ‘You shall love your neighbor as yourself.’</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">like it</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> There is not another commandment greater than these.”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Leviticus 19:18</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 12:32"/>And the scribe said to Him, “Right, Teacher; You have spoken according to truth that He is One and <char style="add">that</char> there is not another besides Him, <verse eid="MRK 12:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 12:33"/>and to love Him out of all the heart and out of all the understanding<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and out of all the soul</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and out of all the strength, and to love the neighbor as oneself is more than all the burnt offerings and sacrifices.” <verse eid="MRK 12:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 12:34"/>And Jesus, having seen him that he answered wisely, said to him, <char style="wj">“You are not far from the kingdom of God.”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 12:34">And no one dared to question Him <char style="add">any</char> longer. <verse eid="MRK 12:34"/></para>

<para style="s">Whose Son Is the Christ?Matthew 22:41–46</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 12:35"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 20:41–44</char></note>And answering, Jesus was saying, teaching in the temple,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char></note> <char style="wj">“How do the scribes say that the Christ is the Son of David? </char><verse eid="MRK 12:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 12:36"/><char style="wj">David himself said in the Holy Spirit: </char></para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 12:36">‘The Lord said to my Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 12:36">“Sit at My right hand </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 12:36">until I place Your enemies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 12:36"><char style="add">as</char> a footstool for Your feet.”’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 110:1</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 12:37"/>David<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Therefore David</char></note> himself calls Him ‘Lord.’ And from where is He his son?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 12:37">And the great crowd was listening to Him gladly. <verse eid="MRK 12:37"/></para>

<para style="s">Beware of the ScribesLuke 20:45–47</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 12:38"/>And in His teaching He was saying,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to them</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <char style="wj">“Beware of the scribes, who are wanting to walk about in long robes and greetings in the marketplaces, </char><verse eid="MRK 12:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 12:39"/><char style="wj">and first seats in the synagogues, and first places at the suppers— </char><verse eid="MRK 12:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 12:40"/><char style="wj">those devouring the houses of widows and praying long as a pretext. These will receive more abundant judgment.”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">defrauding widows of their houses</char></note><verse eid="MRK 12:40"/></para>

<para style="s">The Widow’s OfferingLuke 21:1–4</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 12:41"/>And having sat down opposite the treasury, He was watching how the crowd casts money into the treasury; and many rich ones were casting <char style="add">in</char> much. <verse eid="MRK 12:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 12:42"/>And having come, one poor widow cast <char style="add">in</char> two lepta, which is a kodrantes.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">put in two small copper coins, which amounted to a small fraction of a denarius</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; a lepton was a Jewish coin of bronze or copper worth about 1/128 of a denarius.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 12:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 12:43"/>And having summoned His disciples, He said to them, <char style="wj">“Truly I say to you⁺ that this poor widow cast in more than all of those casting into the treasury. </char><verse eid="MRK 12:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 12:44"/><char style="wj">For all cast in out of that which is abounding to them, but she out of her poverty cast in all, as much as she had—her whole livelihood.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 12:44"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="MRK 13"/>

<para style="s">Temple Destruction and Other Signs</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 13:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 21:5–9</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 24:1–8</char></note>And <char style="add">on</char> His going forth out of the temple, one of His disciples says to Him, “Teacher, behold what stones and what buildings!” <verse eid="MRK 13:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 13:2"/>And Jesus said to him,” <char style="wj">“Do you see these great buildings? Not one stone here shall be left upon a stone that shall not be thrown down.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 13:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 13:3"/>And <char style="add">in</char> His sitting at the Mount of Olives opposite the temple, Peter and James and John and Andrew were questioning Him by Himself, <verse eid="MRK 13:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 13:4"/>“Tell us when these things will be, and what <char style="add">is</char> the sign when all these things are about to be accomplished?” <verse eid="MRK 13:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 13:5"/>And<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">answering</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Jesus began to say to them, <char style="wj">“Take heed, lest anyone may lead you⁺ astray. </char><verse eid="MRK 13:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 13:6"/><char style="wj">Many</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For many</char></note><char style="wj"> will come in My name, saying, ‘I am He,’ and they will lead many astray. </char><verse eid="MRK 13:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 13:7"/><char style="wj">And when you⁺ shall hear of wars and rumors of wars, do not be alarmed. It is necessary</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For it is necessary</char></note><char style="wj"> to happen, but the end is not yet. </char><verse eid="MRK 13:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 13:8"/><char style="wj">For nation will rise up against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be earthquakes in various places; there will be famines.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and riots</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> These are the beginning of birth pains. </char><verse eid="MRK 13:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Witnessing to All NationsMatthew 24:9–14</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 13:9"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 21:10–19</char></note>But you⁺, take heed to yourselves. They will deliver<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For they will deliver</char></note> you⁺ up to courts, and you⁺ will be beaten in synagogues, and you⁺ will stand before governors and kings on account of Me, for a testimony to them. <verse eid="MRK 13:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 13:10"/>And to all the nations first it is necessary for the gospel to be proclaimed. <verse eid="MRK 13:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 13:11"/>But when they might lead you⁺ away, delivering <char style="add">you</char> up, do not be anxious beforehand<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">or premeditate</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> what you⁺ shall speak; but whatever might be given to you⁺ in that hour, speak that. For you⁺ are not the ones speaking, but the Holy Spirit. <verse eid="MRK 13:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 13:12"/>And brother will deliver up brother to death, and father, child; and children will rise up against parents and will put them to death. <verse eid="MRK 13:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 13:13"/>And you⁺ will be hated by all because of My name; but the one having endured to the end, he will be saved. <verse eid="MRK 13:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Abomination of DesolationMatthew 24:15–25</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 13:14"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 21:20–24</char></note>But when you⁺ shall see the ‘abomination of the desolation’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Daniel 9:27, Daniel 11:31, and Daniel 12:11; BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">spoken of by Daniel the prophet</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> standing where it should not<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">where he should not</char></note> (the one reading, let him understand), then those in Judea, let them flee to the mountains; <verse eid="MRK 13:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 13:15"/>and the one upon the housetop, let him not come down nor go in<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nor go inside the house</char></note> to take up anything out of his house; <verse eid="MRK 13:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 13:16"/>and the one in the field, let him not return to the things behind to take away his garment. <verse eid="MRK 13:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 13:17"/>And woe to those having in womb and to those nursing in those days! <verse eid="MRK 13:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 13:18"/>And pray that it<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">pray that your flight</char></note> might not be in winter, <verse eid="MRK 13:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 13:19"/>for those days will be tribulation such as has not been from the beginning of creation that God created until now, and never shall be. <verse eid="MRK 13:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 13:20"/>And if the Lord did not shorten the days, not any flesh would have been saved; but because of the chosen whom He chose, He shortened the days. <verse eid="MRK 13:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 13:21"/>And then if anyone shall say to you⁺, ‘Behold, here <char style="add">is</char> the Christ!’ <char style="add">or</char> ‘Behold, there!’ do not believe <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="MRK 13:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 13:22"/>For false Christs and false prophets will arise and will give signs and wonders in order to lead astray, if possible, the chosen.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">even the chosen</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 13:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 13:23"/>But you⁺ take heed; I have forewarned<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">see, I have forewarned</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> you⁺ of all things. <verse eid="MRK 13:23"/></para>

<para style="s">The Return of the Son of ManMatthew 24:26–31</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 13:24"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 21:25–28</char></note>But in those days, after that tribulation: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 13:24">‘The sun will be darkened, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 13:24">and the moon will not give her light; <verse eid="MRK 13:24"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 13:25"/>and the stars will be falling out of the sky, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 13:25">and the powers that <char style="add">are</char> in the heavens will be shaken.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the celestial bodies will be shaken</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Isaiah 13:10, Isaiah 34:4, and Joel 2:10.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 13:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 13:26"/>And then they will see the Son of Man coming in the clouds with great power and glory. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Daniel 7:13–14.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 13:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 13:27"/>And then He will send the angels,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His angels</char></note> and He will gather together His chosen from the four winds, from the end of earth to the end of heaven. <verse eid="MRK 13:27"/></para>

<para style="s">The Lesson of the Fig TreeMatthew 24:32–35</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 13:28"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 21:29–33</char></note>And from the fig tree, learn the parable:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">this lesson</char></note> When its branch already shall have become tender, and it puts forth leaves, you⁺ know<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">one knows</char></note> that summer is near. <verse eid="MRK 13:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 13:29"/>So also you⁺, when you⁺ see these things coming to pass, know that He is near,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">it is near</char></note> at the doors. <verse eid="MRK 13:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 13:30"/>Truly I say to you⁺ that this generation shall not have passed away until all these things shall have come to pass. <verse eid="MRK 13:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 13:31"/>The heaven and the earth will pass away, but My words will never pass away. <verse eid="MRK 13:31"/></para>

<para style="s">Readiness at Any HourMatthew 24:36–51</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 13:32"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 12:35–48</char></note>But concerning that day or<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and</char></note> hour no one knows, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, except the Father. <verse eid="MRK 13:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 13:33"/>Take heed; stay awake!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Take heed, watch, and pray!</char></note> For you⁺ do not know when the time is. <verse eid="MRK 13:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 13:34"/><char style="add">It is</char> like a man going on a journey, having left his house and having given his servants authority, to each his work. And he commanded the doorkeeper that he should watch. <verse eid="MRK 13:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 13:35"/>Therefore watch, for you⁺ do not know when the master of the house comes—either at evening, or at midnight, or when the rooster crows, or morning— <verse eid="MRK 13:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 13:36"/>lest, having come suddenly, he should find you⁺ sleeping. <verse eid="MRK 13:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 13:37"/>And what I say to you⁺, I say to all: Watch!” <verse eid="MRK 13:37"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="MRK 14"/>

<para style="s">The Plot to Kill Jesus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 14:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 11:45–57</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:1–2</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 26:1–5</char></note>And after two days it would be the Passover and the Unleavened.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the Feast of Unleavened Bread</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 12:14–20.</char></note> And the chief priests and the scribes were seeking how, having taken Him by stealth, they might kill <char style="add">Him</char>. <verse eid="MRK 14:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 14:2"/>For they were saying, “Not during the feast, lest there will be an uproar of the people.” <verse eid="MRK 14:2"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Anointed at BethanyMatthew 26:6–13</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 14:3"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 12:1–8</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 7:36–50</char></note>And of Him being in Bethany in the house of Simon the Leper,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Aramaic </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Simon the Potter</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Simon the Jar Maker</char></note> <char style="add">at</char> His having reclined, a woman came, having an alabaster flask of fragrant oil of pure nard of great price. Having broken the alabaster flask, she poured <char style="add">it</char> on His head. <verse eid="MRK 14:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 14:4"/>And some were indignant within themselves:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and said</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> “Why has this waste of the fragrant oil come to pass? <verse eid="MRK 14:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 14:5"/>For this fragrant oil could have been sold for more than three hundred denarii<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A denarius was customarily a day’s wage for a laborer; see Matthew 20:2.</char></note> and given to the poor.” And they were grumbling at her. <verse eid="MRK 14:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 14:6"/>And Jesus said, <char style="wj">“Leave her alone; why do you⁺ cause trouble to her? She did a good work toward Me. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 14:7"/><char style="wj">For the poor you⁺ always have with you,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Deuteronomy 15:11.</char></note><char style="wj"> and you⁺ are able to do them good whenever you⁺ desire; but not always do you⁺ have Me. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 14:8"/><char style="wj">She did what she could. She came beforehand to anoint My body for the burial. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 14:9"/><char style="wj">And truly I say to you⁺, wherever the gospel</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">this gospel</char></note><char style="wj"> shall be proclaimed in the whole world, what this woman did also will be spoken of, for a memorial of her.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Judas Agrees to Betray JesusMatthew 26:14–16</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 14:10"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:3–6</char></note>And Judas Iscariot, one of the Twelve, went away to the chief priests, so that he might betray Him to them. <verse eid="MRK 14:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 14:11"/>And having heard, they rejoiced and promised to give him silver. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 14:11">And he was seeking how he might deliver Him up opportunely. <verse eid="MRK 14:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Preparing the PassoverMatthew 26:17–19</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 14:12"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:7–13</char></note>And on the first day of the Unleavened,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">On the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 12:14–20.</char></note> when they were to sacrifice the Passover, His disciples say to Him, “Where do You desire <char style="add">that</char>, having gone, we should prepare so that You may eat the Passover?” <verse eid="MRK 14:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 14:13"/>And He sends forth two of His disciples and says to them, <char style="wj">“Go into the city, and a man carrying a pitcher of water will meet you⁺. Follow him. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 14:14"/><char style="wj">And wherever he might enter, say to the master of the house that the Teacher says, ‘Where is My guest room,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the guest room</char></note><char style="wj"> where I may eat the Passover with My disciples?’ </char><verse eid="MRK 14:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 14:15"/><char style="wj">And he will show you⁺ a large upper room, having been furnished, prepared. And prepare for us there.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 14:16"/>And the disciples<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His disciples</char></note> went away, and they came into the city, and they found <char style="add">it</char> as He said to them, and they prepared the Passover. <verse eid="MRK 14:16"/></para>

<para style="s">The Last SupperMatthew 26:20–30</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 14:17"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 11:17–34</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:14–23</char></note>And evening having come, He comes with the Twelve. <verse eid="MRK 14:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 14:18"/>And <char style="add">in</char> their reclining and eating, Jesus said, <char style="wj">“Truly I say to you⁺ that one of you⁺ who is eating with Me will betray Me.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 14:19"/>They began to be grieved and to say to Him one by one, “Surely not I?”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And another, “Is it I?”</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 14:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 14:20"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“One of the Twelve, the one dipping</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the one who is dipping his hand</char></note><char style="wj"> into the bowl with Me. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 14:21"/><char style="wj">For indeed, the Son of Man goes as it has been written concerning Him; but woe to that man by whom the Son of Man is betrayed! It were better for him if that man had not been born.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 14:22"/>And <char style="add">in</char> their eating, having taken bread, having spoken a blessing, He broke <char style="add">it</char> and gave to them and said, <char style="wj">“Take;</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Take, eat</char></note><char style="wj"> this is My body.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 14:23"/>And having taken the cup, having given thanks, He gave to them, and they all drank of it. <verse eid="MRK 14:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 14:24"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“This is My blood of the covenant,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the new covenant</char></note><char style="wj"> which is being poured out for many. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 14:25"/><char style="wj">Truly I say to you⁺ that I will never again drink of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it anew in the kingdom of God.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 14:26"/>And having sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives. <verse eid="MRK 14:26"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Predicts Peter’s DenialZechariah 13:7–9</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 14:27"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 13:36–38</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:31–38</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 26:31–35</char></note>And Jesus says to them, <char style="wj">“You⁺ will all fall away,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on account of Me this night</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 26:31.</char></note><char style="wj"> for it has been written: </char></para>

<para style="q1" vid="MRK 14:27">‘I will strike the shepherd, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="MRK 14:27">and the sheep will be scattered.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Zechariah 13:7</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 14:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="MRK 14:28"/>But after having arisen, I will go before you⁺ into Galilee.” <verse eid="MRK 14:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 14:29"/>But Peter was saying to Him, “Even if all will fall away, yet not I.” <verse eid="MRK 14:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 14:30"/>And Jesus says to him, <char style="wj">“Truly I say to you that now, this night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 14:31"/>But he kept saying emphatically, “If it is needful of me to die with You, never will I deny You.” And all of them were saying likewise also. <verse eid="MRK 14:31"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Prays at GethsemaneMatthew 26:36–46</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 14:32"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:39–46</char></note>And they come to a place, the name of which <char style="add">is</char> Gethsemane; and He says to His disciples, <char style="wj">“Sit here until I may pray.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 14:33"/>And He takes Peter and James and John with Him, and He began to be greatly awestruck and deeply distressed. <verse eid="MRK 14:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 14:34"/>And He says to them, <char style="wj">“My soul is very sorrowful, even to death. Remain here and watch.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 14:35"/>And having gone forward a little, He fell upon the ground and was praying that, if it is possible, the hour might pass from Him. <verse eid="MRK 14:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 14:36"/>And He was saying, <char style="wj">“Abba, Father, all things are possible to You. Take away this cup from Me. But not what I will, but what You will.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 14:37"/>And He comes and finds them sleeping, and He says to Peter, <char style="wj">“Simon, are you asleep? Were you not able to watch one hour? </char><verse eid="MRK 14:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 14:38"/><char style="wj">Watch and pray, so that you⁺ may not enter into temptation. For the spirit is willing, but the flesh weak.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 14:39"/>And again, having gone away, He prayed, having said the same thing. <verse eid="MRK 14:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 14:40"/>And again having come, He found them sleeping. For their eyes were heavy, and they did not know what they should answer Him. <verse eid="MRK 14:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 14:41"/>And He comes the third time and says to them, <char style="wj">“Are you⁺ still sleeping and resting? It is enough! The hour came. Behold, the Son of Man is delivered up into the hands of the sinful. </char><verse eid="MRK 14:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 14:42"/><char style="wj">Rise, let us go. Behold, the one betraying Me has drawn near!”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:42"/></para>

<para style="s">The Betrayal of JesusMatthew 26:47–56</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 14:43"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 18:1–14</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:47–53</char></note>And immediately, <char style="add">in</char> His still speaking, Judas,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Judas Iscariot</char></note> one of the Twelve, comes up, and with Him a crowd<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a large crowd</char></note> with swords and clubs, from the chief priests and the scribes and the elders. <verse eid="MRK 14:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 14:44"/>Now the one delivering Him up had given to them a sign, saying, “Whomever I shall kiss is He; seize Him and lead <char style="add">Him</char> away securely.” <verse eid="MRK 14:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 14:45"/>And having come, immediately having come near to Him, he says, “Rabbi!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.45 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Rabbi, Rabbi!”</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Greetings, Rabbi!”</char></note>” And he kissed Him. <verse eid="MRK 14:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="MRK 14:46"/>And they laid the hands on Him and seized Him. <verse eid="MRK 14:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="MRK 14:47"/>And a certain one of those standing by, having drawn the sword, struck the servant of the high priest and cut off his ear. <verse eid="MRK 14:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="MRK 14:48"/>And Jesus, answering, said to them, <char style="wj">“Did you⁺ come out with swords and clubs, as against a robber, to capture Me? </char><verse eid="MRK 14:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="MRK 14:49"/><char style="wj">Every day I was with you⁺ in the temple,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.49 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char></note><char style="wj"> teaching, and you⁺ did not seize Me. But it is so that the Scriptures may be fulfilled.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 14:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="MRK 14:50"/>And all, having left Him, fled. <verse eid="MRK 14:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="MRK 14:51"/>And a certain young man was following Him, having cast a linen cloth about <char style="add">his</char> naked <char style="add">body</char>. And they seize<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.51 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And the young men seize</char></note> him, <verse eid="MRK 14:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="MRK 14:52"/>and having left behind the linen cloth, he fled<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.52 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from them</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> naked. <verse eid="MRK 14:52"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus before the SanhedrinMatthew 26:57–68</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="MRK 14:53"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 18:19–24</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:66–71</char></note>And they led away Jesus to the high priest, and all the chief priests and the elders and the scribes come together.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.53 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with him</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 14:53"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="MRK 14:54"/>And Peter followed Him from afar off, as far as to within the court of the high priest. And he was sitting with the officers and warming himself at the fire. <verse eid="MRK 14:54"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="MRK 14:55"/>And the chief priests and all the Council<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.55 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the whole Sanhedrin</char></note> were seeking testimony against Jesus to put Him to death, but they were not finding <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="MRK 14:55"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="MRK 14:56"/>For many were bearing false testimony against Him, but their testimonies were not alike. <verse eid="MRK 14:56"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="MRK 14:57"/>And some, having risen up, were bearing false testimony against Him, saying, <verse eid="MRK 14:57"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="MRK 14:58"/>“We heard Him saying, ‘I will demolish this temple made with hands, and in three days I will build another, not made with hands.’” <verse eid="MRK 14:58"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="MRK 14:59"/>And not even in this matter was their testimony alike. <verse eid="MRK 14:59"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="MRK 14:60"/>And the high priest, having risen up in the midst, questioned Jesus, saying, “Do You not answer? What do these testify against You?” <verse eid="MRK 14:60"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="MRK 14:61"/>But He was silent and did not answer. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 14:61">Again the high priest was questioning Him and says to Him, “Are You the Christ, the Son of the Blessed One?” <verse eid="MRK 14:61"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="MRK 14:62"/>And Jesus said, <char style="wj">“I am. And you⁺ will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power and coming with the clouds of heaven.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.62 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the right hand of the Mighty One</char></note><char style="wj">”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.62 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Psalm 110:1 and Daniel 7:13.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 14:62"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="MRK 14:63"/>And the high priest, having torn his garments, says, “What more need do we have of witnesses? <verse eid="MRK 14:63"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="MRK 14:64"/>You⁺ heard the blasphemy. What does it appear to you⁺?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 14:64">And all condemned Him to be deserving of death. <verse eid="MRK 14:64"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="MRK 14:65"/>And some began to spit upon Him and to cover up His face and to strike Him and to say to Him, “Prophesy!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.65 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Prophesy to us! Who hit You?”</char></note>” And the officers received Him<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.65 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">kept striking Him</char></note> with slaps. <verse eid="MRK 14:65"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter Denies JesusMatthew 26:69–75</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="MRK 14:66"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 18:15–18</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:54–62</char></note>And of Peter being below in the courtyard, one of the servant girls of the high priest comes, <verse eid="MRK 14:66"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="MRK 14:67"/>and having seen Peter warming himself, having looked at him, she says, “You also were with the Nazarene, Jesus.” <verse eid="MRK 14:67"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="MRK 14:68"/>But he denied <char style="add">it</char>, saying, “I neither know nor understand what you say.” And he went forth out into the gateway, and the rooster crowed. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.68 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE and WH do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and the rooster crowed</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 14:68"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="MRK 14:69"/>And the servant girl, having seen him, began to say again to those standing by, “This is one of them.” <verse eid="MRK 14:69"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="MRK 14:70"/>But he denied <char style="add">it</char> again. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 14:70">And after a little while, again those standing by were saying to Peter, “Truly you are of them, for you also are a Galilean.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.70 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and your speech is similar</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 14:70"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="MRK 14:71"/>But he began to curse and to swear, “I do not know this man of whom you⁺ speak!” <verse eid="MRK 14:71"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="MRK 14:72"/>And immediately a rooster<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">14.72 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And a rooster</char></note> crowed for the second time. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 14:72">And Peter remembered the word that Jesus said to him: <char style="wj">“Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”</char> And having broken down, he began to weep. <verse eid="MRK 14:72"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="MRK 15"/>

<para style="s">Jesus Delivered to Pilate</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 15:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:1–2</char></note>And early in the morning, having formed a counsel, the chief priests, with the elders and scribes and the whole Council,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the whole Sanhedrin</char></note> having bound Jesus, led <char style="add">Him</char> away and delivered <char style="add">Him</char> to Pilate. <verse eid="MRK 15:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 15:2"/>And Pilate questioned Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 15:2">And answering, He says to him, <char style="wj">“You say.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 15:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 15:3"/>And the chief priests were accusing Him harshly.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC and Scrivener TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">but He gave no answer</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 15:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 15:4"/>And Pilate began to question Him again, saying, “Do You not answer? See how many things they are accusing You of!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">testifying against You</char></note>” <verse eid="MRK 15:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 15:5"/>But Jesus answered no more, so as to amaze Pilate. <verse eid="MRK 15:5"/></para>

<para style="s">The Crowd Chooses BarabbasMatthew 27:15–23</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 15:6"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:13–25</char></note>Now at the feast he would release to them<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Now it was Pilate's custom at the feast to release to the people</char></note> one prisoner whom they requested. <verse eid="MRK 15:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 15:7"/>And the one called Barabbas was there, having been bound with the rebels<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">his fellow rebels</char></note> who had committed murder in the insurrection. <verse eid="MRK 15:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 15:8"/>And the crowd, having gone up,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having cried out</char></note> began to request <char style="add">that which</char> he usually did for them. <verse eid="MRK 15:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 15:9"/>But Pilate answered them, saying, “Do you⁺ desire <char style="add">that</char> I should release to you⁺ the King of the Jews?” <verse eid="MRK 15:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 15:10"/>For he was aware that the chief priests had delivered Him up because of envy. <verse eid="MRK 15:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 15:11"/>But the chief priests stirred up the crowd so that he might release to them Barabbas instead. <verse eid="MRK 15:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Pilate Delivers Up JesusMatthew 27:24–26</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 15:12"/>And Pilate, answering, was saying to them again, “Then what do you⁺ desire <char style="add">that</char> I should do<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, TH, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Then what should I do</char></note> with the One whom you⁺ call the King of the Jews?” <verse eid="MRK 15:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 15:13"/>And they cried out again, “Crucify Him!” <verse eid="MRK 15:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 15:14"/>And Pilate was saying to them, “Why? What evil did He commit?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 15:14">But they shouted much more, “Crucify Him!” <verse eid="MRK 15:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 15:15"/>And Pilate, desiring to do that which <char style="add">was</char> satisfactory to the crowd, released Barabbas to them. And having flogged <char style="add">Him</char>, he delivered up Jesus so that He might be crucified. <verse eid="MRK 15:15"/></para>

<para style="s">The Soldiers Mock JesusIsaiah 50:4–11</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 15:16"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 19:1–15</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 22:63–65</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:27–31</char></note>And the soldiers led Him away into the palace (that is, the Praetorium), and they call together the whole cohort. <verse eid="MRK 15:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 15:17"/>And they put on Him purple, and having twisted together a crown of thorns, they placed <char style="add">it</char> on Him. <verse eid="MRK 15:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 15:18"/>And they began to salute Him:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saying</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> “Hail, King of the Jews!” <verse eid="MRK 15:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 15:19"/>And they kept striking His head with a reed and spitting on Him. And bending the knees, they were kneeling down to Him. <verse eid="MRK 15:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 15:20"/>And when they had mocked Him, they took off of Him the purple and put on Him His own garments. And they are leading Him out so that they might crucify Him. <verse eid="MRK 15:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The CrucifixionPsalm 22:1–31</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="MRK 15:21"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 19:16–27</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:26–43</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:32–44</char></note>And they compel one passing by, Simon of Cyrene, the father of Alexander and Rufus, coming from the country, that he might carry His cross. <verse eid="MRK 15:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="MRK 15:22"/>And they bring Him to a place, Golgotha, which is translated, Place of a Skull. <verse eid="MRK 15:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="MRK 15:23"/>And they were offering Him wine<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to drink</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> having been mixed with gall, but He did not take <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="MRK 15:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="MRK 15:24"/>And they crucify Him. </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 15:24">And they divide His garments, casting a lot for them, who should take what. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Psalm 22:18.</char></note><verse eid="MRK 15:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="MRK 15:25"/>And it was the third hour,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, nine in the morning</char></note> and they crucified Him. <verse eid="MRK 15:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="MRK 15:26"/>And there was the inscription of the accusation against Him, having been written: </para>

<para style="p" vid="MRK 15:26">THE KING OF THE JEWS.<verse eid="MRK 15:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="MRK 15:27"/>And with Him they crucify two robbers,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">insurrectionists</char></note> one at <char style="add">His</char> right hand and one at His left.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">28</char><char style="fq" closed="false">So the Scripture was fulfilled that says, “And He was numbered with the transgressors.”</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Isaiah 53:12 and Luke 22:37.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 15:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="MRK 15:29"/>And those passing by were railing at Him, shaking their heads and saying, “Aha! The One demolishing the temple and building <char style="add">it</char> in three days, <verse eid="MRK 15:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="MRK 15:30"/>save Yourself, having come down from the cross!” <verse eid="MRK 15:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="MRK 15:31"/>Likewise also the chief priests, with the scribes, mocking among one another, were saying, “He saved others; Himself He is not able to save! <verse eid="MRK 15:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="MRK 15:32"/>The Christ, the King of Israel, let Him come down now from the cross, that we might see and believe!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">believe Him</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note>” And those being crucified with Him were upbraiding Him. <verse eid="MRK 15:32"/></para>

<para style="s">The Death of JesusPsalm 22:1–31</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="MRK 15:33"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 19:28–30</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:44–49</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:45–56</char></note>And the sixth hour<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, noon </char></note> having come, darkness came over all the land until the ninth hour.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, three in the afternoon</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 15:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="MRK 15:34"/>And at the ninth hour, Jesus cried out in a loud voice, <char style="wj">“Eloi, Eloi, lema sabachthani?”</char> which is translated, <char style="wj">“My God, My God, why did You forsake Me?”</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">lima</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; TR, TH, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">lamma</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 22:1</char></note><verse eid="MRK 15:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="MRK 15:35"/>And some of those standing by, having heard, were saying, “Behold, He calls Elijah.” <verse eid="MRK 15:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="MRK 15:36"/>And one, having run and having filled a sponge with vinegar,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a sponge with wine vinegar</char></note> having put <char style="add">it</char> on a reed, gave Him to drink,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Psalm 69:21.</char></note> saying, “Let <char style="add">Him</char> be; let us see if Elijah comes to take Him down.” <verse eid="MRK 15:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="MRK 15:37"/>But Jesus, having uttered a great cry, breathed His last. <verse eid="MRK 15:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="MRK 15:38"/>And the veil of the temple was torn into two from top to bottom. <verse eid="MRK 15:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="MRK 15:39"/>And the centurion standing opposite of Him, having seen that in this way He breathed His last,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having seen that, having cried out, He breathed His last</char></note> said, “Truly this man was the Son of God!” <verse eid="MRK 15:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="MRK 15:40"/>And there were also women looking on from afar off, among whom also <char style="add">were</char> Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joses</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is a variant of </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joseph</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Matthew 27:56.</char></note> and Salome, <verse eid="MRK 15:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="MRK 15:41"/>who had been following Him and had been ministering to Him when He was in Galilee, and many others, those having come up with Him to Jerusalem. <verse eid="MRK 15:41"/></para>

<para style="s">The Burial of JesusIsaiah 53:9–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="MRK 15:42"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 19:38–42</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 23:50–56</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 27:57–61</char></note>And evening already having come, since it was the Preparation (that is, the day before the Sabbath), <verse eid="MRK 15:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="MRK 15:43"/>having come, Joseph from Arimathea, a prominent Council member who was also himself waiting for the kingdom of God, having boldness, went in to Pilate and asked for the body of Jesus. <verse eid="MRK 15:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="MRK 15:44"/>And Pilate wondered if already He was dead.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">had been dead for some time</char></note> And having summoned the centurion, he inquired of him whether He was dead already. <verse eid="MRK 15:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="MRK 15:45"/>And having known from the centurion, he granted the body to Joseph. <verse eid="MRK 15:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="MRK 15:46"/>And having bought a linen cloth, having taken Him down, he wrapped <char style="add">Him</char> in the linen cloth and laid Him in a tomb that was cut out of a rock. And he rolled a stone to the door of the tomb. <verse eid="MRK 15:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="MRK 15:47"/>And Mary Magdalene and Mary the <char style="add">mother</char> of Joses<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joseph</char></note> were watching where He was laid. <verse eid="MRK 15:47"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="MRK 16"/>

<para style="s">The Resurrection</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="MRK 16:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">John 20:1–9</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 24:1–12</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Matthew 28:1–10</char></note>And <char style="add">on</char> the Sabbath having passed, Mary Magdalene and Mary the <char style="add">mother</char> of James and Salome bought spices so that, having come, they might anoint Him. <verse eid="MRK 16:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="MRK 16:2"/>And very early on the first of the Sabbaths,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">very early on the first day of the week,</char></note> they come to the tomb <char style="add">at</char> the sun having arisen. <verse eid="MRK 16:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="MRK 16:3"/>And they were saying among themselves, “Who will roll away the stone for us out from the door of the tomb?” <verse eid="MRK 16:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="MRK 16:4"/>And having looked up, they see that the stone has been rolled away—for it was exceedingly large. <verse eid="MRK 16:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="MRK 16:5"/>And having entered into the tomb, they saw a young man clothed in a white robe sitting on the right, and they were greatly amazed. <verse eid="MRK 16:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="MRK 16:6"/>Now he says to them, “Do not be amazed. You⁺ seek Jesus the Nazarene, the One having been crucified. He is risen! He is not here! Behold the place where they laid Him. <verse eid="MRK 16:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="MRK 16:7"/>But go, say to His disciples and to Peter, ‘He goes before you⁺ into Galilee. There you⁺ will see Him, as He said to you⁺.’” <verse eid="MRK 16:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="MRK 16:8"/>And having gone out, they fled<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">ran away quickly</char></note> from the tomb, for trembling and amazement had seized them. And they spoke nothing to <char style="add">anyone</char>, for they were afraid.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Some manuscripts end the Gospel of Mark after verse 8. Other manuscripts contain only a short ending, a version of the following: </char><char style="fq" closed="false">9</char><char style="fq" closed="false">But they quickly reported all these instructions to Peter’s companions. Afterward, Jesus Himself, through them, sent out from east to west the sacred and imperishable proclamation of eternal salvation. Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 16:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Appears to Mary MagdaleneJohn 20:10–18</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="MRK 16:9"/>And having risen early <char style="add">on</char> the first of the week,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Early on the first day of the week, after Jesus had risen,</char></note> He appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom He had cast out seven demons. <verse eid="MRK 16:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="MRK 16:10"/>She, having gone, reported to those having been with Him, mourning and weeping. <verse eid="MRK 16:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="MRK 16:11"/>And they, having heard that He is alive and was seen by her, disbelieved. <verse eid="MRK 16:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Jesus Appears to Two DisciplesLuke 24:13–35</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="MRK 16:12"/>And after these things, He appeared in another form to two of them as they are walking, going into the country. <verse eid="MRK 16:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="MRK 16:13"/>And they, having gone, reported to the rest; neither did they believe them. <verse eid="MRK 16:13"/></para>

<para style="s">The Great CommissionMatthew 28:16–20</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="MRK 16:14"/>And afterward, <char style="add">in</char> their reclining, He appeared to the Eleven and rebuked their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they did not believe those having seen Him arisen.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">risen from the dead</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 16:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="MRK 16:15"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“Having gone into all the world, proclaim the gospel to all the creation. </char><verse eid="MRK 16:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="MRK 16:16"/><char style="wj">The one having believed and having been baptized will be saved, but the one having disbelieved will be condemned. </char><verse eid="MRK 16:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="MRK 16:17"/><char style="wj">And these signs will accompany</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TH and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">will follow</char></note><char style="wj"> those having believed: In My name they will cast out demons; they will speak with new tongues;</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in tongues</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="MRK 16:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="MRK 16:18"/><char style="wj">and with their hands</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with their hands</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> they will take up serpents; and if they drink anything deadly, it shall never hurt them; they will lay hands upon the sick, and they will be well.”</char> <verse eid="MRK 16:18"/></para>

<para style="s">The AscensionLuke 24:50–53</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="MRK 16:19"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 1:6–11</char></note>Therefore indeed the Lord Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Most BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord</char></note> after speaking to them, was taken up into heaven and sat at the right hand of God. <verse eid="MRK 16:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="MRK 16:20"/>And they, having gone out, preached everywhere, the Lord working with <char style="add">them</char> and confirming the word by the accompanying signs.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Amen.</char></note> <verse eid="MRK 16:20"/></para>

<chapter eid="MRK 16"/>

</usx>
